\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10512\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/23: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is showing signs of profit booking, resulting in a slight downturn in altcoin prices.\par \par \uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crypto announcement acted as a trigger that drove Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price to a new 52-week high. During such news-based events, traders holding short positions are caught off guard and are forced to cover their trades, resulting in the type of short squeeze seen during the Oct. 21 rally.\par \par \uc2 However, after this initial burst, the next leg of the uptrend is only possible if demand picks up and the bulls continue to buy at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 Data from Huobi exchange suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-key-metrics-and-disinterest-from-pro-traders-hint-at-bitcoin-price-sell-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro traders are not convinced that the current rally warrants the opening of long positions}}}\uc2  and Cointelegraph contributor Marcel Pechman explained that this could be a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/a5ae922c-4e47-4b82-82ae-2a427bf04ce4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-frenzy-cme-becomes-2nd-biggest-bitcoin-futures-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open interest}}}\uc2  on CME Bitcoin futures paints a different picture. The CME has now become the second biggest Bitcoin futures exchange in terms of open interest, second only to OKEx. This suggests that institutional demand could be picking up.\par \par \uc2 This opposing set of data from Bitcoin futures exchanges only adds to the confusion among traders about the next possible move.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s go a little deep into the psychology of the traders for a better understanding. Institutional investors rarely buy because of FOMO as they are generally more averse to\par \par \uc2 These large traders may wait for the rally to sustain and complete a successful retest of the breakout level before buying.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the top-10 cryptocurrencies in order to determine what the technical indicators project.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above the $12,460 resistance on Oct. 21. This move helped the cryptocurrency notch a new 52-week high, which is a sign of strength.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/85c6ab1d-ab7a-42f0-b00c-1f357790bfdc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($11,679) is sloping up and the 50-day simple moving average ($10,943) has also started to rise. This shows that both the short-term and the medium-term trend favors the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, the rally above $13,000 pushed the relative strength index close to 81, a level which attracted profit booking the last two times it was reached.\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair is facing selling above $13,000 but the bulls do not seem to be in a hurry to close their positions. If the pair does not drop below $12,460 within the next few days, it will increase the possibility of a rally to $14,000.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bears can pull the price below the $12,460\u8211\'20\'13$12,050 support zone, it will suggest a lack of demand at higher levels. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bear trap.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above $395 on Oct. 22. This move completed the ascending triangle pattern, which has a target objective of $478.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/927b02dc-e44c-49a3-92b7-4bf18089fdfe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($377) and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are currently trying to pull the price back below the breakout level of $395. If they succeed, it will signal that the current breakout was a fake one. The next support on the downside is the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the ETH/USD pair rebounds off $395, it will suggest that the breakout is valid. The uptrend could pick up momentum after the bulls push the price above $421.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  attempted to rise above the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.26 range on Oct. 21 but the bulls could not close the price above $0.26. This suggests a lack of buyers at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/324fb92a-f552-45f4-a774-5634efa358b9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure of the XRP/USD pair to break out of the range could have attracted profit booking. If the price breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest that the range-bound action is likely to extend for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($0.24), the bulls will once again attempt to drive the pair above the $0.26\u8211\'20\'13$0.265763 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above the resistance zone will complete an inverted head and shoulders pattern that could signal the start of a new uptrend with a target objective of $0.30.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) is currently facing selling near the overhead resistance at $280. This shows that the bears are trying to keep the price below this level. If they succeed, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($247) is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/6f23e6dc-c03b-4faf-8386-3a172d661d9b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the oversold zone suggest that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $280, a move to $300 is possible. This level could act as resistance but if the bulls can thrust the price above it, the BCH/USD pair could resume the uptrend and reach $326.30\u8211\'20\'13$337.90.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the critical support at $242.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the downtrend line on Oct. 22. This suggests that the correction could be over. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 56 suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/618dddf6-7b3e-46ab-b81c-14baffe5bfcb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $31.9798, a retest of the 52-week high at $33.3888 is possible. A breakout and close above this level could resume the uptrend that can challenge the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price continues to decline from the current levels and plummet below $28.50. Such a move could start a deeper correction to $22.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) completed an ascending triangle pattern when it broke and closed above $11.8028 on Oct. 22. The target objective of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup is $15.\par \par \uc2 The gradually upsloping 20-day EMA ($10.71) and the RSI above 57 suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/c34a5af9-66e5-44f5-a6df-5b7cd4e8189d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are not willing to let bulls have their way. They are currently attempting to drag the price back below the $11.199\u8211\'20\'13$11.8028 support zone. If they manage to do that, it will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears fail to sustain the price below the support zone, it will indicate that the bulls are accumulating on dips. This could increase the possibility of a rally to $13.28 and higher.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) closed above the 20-day EMA ($4.17) on Oct. 22. The bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $4.6112. A close above this resistance could drive the price to $5.5899.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e55c8b03-6643-4c85-b5c0-7299f3918086.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has risen above the 50 levels for the first time in more than a month. This suggests that the selling pressure has reduced and the bulls are attempting to make a comeback.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price again slips back below the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USD pair could extend its stay inside the range for a few more days. The pair may turn negative if the bears sink the pair below the critical support at $3.5321.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) completed an inverse head and shoulders pattern when it broke out and closed above the $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 resistance zone. The pattern target of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal setup is $61.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/501c51e1-b8f9-45e8-acb4-8b229a3dba5e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($49) and the RSI near the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 However, after the initial run-up, the price may retest the breakout zone of $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36. If the bulls purchase the dip to this zone and the price recovers sharply, it will suggest that the zone may act as a floor in the future.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears drag and sustain the LTC/USD pair below $51. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside a rising wedge pattern for the past few days. The bulls have failed to push the price above the immediate resistance at $0.1142241, which shows a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/4e039054-a3f2-4f7c-be98-586188cafb02.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising wedge is usually considered as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The pattern will complete when the price drops and closes below the support line of the wedge. Such a move could drag the price down to $0.090 and then to $0.0755701.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA ($0.10) and the RSI in the positive zone suggest a minor advantage to the bulls. If the buyers can propel the price above the wedge, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could start an up-move that may reach $0.01445.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) has formed a symmetrical triangle pattern, which shows indecision among the bulls and the bears. Although the bulls had pushed the price above the triangle on Oct. 22, they could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5f63b269-1eaf-4634-9116-913b89fc683e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price has turned down from the downtrend line and the bears will now try to sink the BSV/USD pair to the uptrend line of the triangle. If this support cracks, a drop to $146.20 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rebounds off the uptrend line, the bulls will once again attempt to push the price above the triangle. If they can pull it off, a rally to $180.63 and then to $227 could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5ldS1jZW50cmFsLTEuYW1hem9uYXdzLmNvbS9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvYzBlZWY4OTQtZDJkZS00NzM1LWExNGItNWQ0OTEwODEwNjAwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201023egan000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/21: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,682 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin hit a new 2020 high and altcoins rallied as \uc2 PayPal\uc2  announced that it will support crypto payments.\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-soars-to-12-9k-as-paypal-proves-crypto-is-ready-for-everyone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheering}}}\uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow its customers to use cryptocurrencies to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-to-offer-crypto-payments-starting-in-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shop}}}\uc2  from its vast merchant network. \uc2 PayPal\uc2  also revealed that U.S. account holders will be able to buy, sell, and hold cryptocurrencies in the \uc2 PayPal\uc2  app.\par \par \uc2 The company plans to extend this service to a few other countries in the first half of 2021. \uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision has significantly increased the reach of cryptocurrencies. Now many of the company\u8217\'20\'19s 346 million active users will have the options to engage with cryptocurrencies and become investors if they choose.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e5966b7d-0b1a-44d2-8f5a-5b87eee0c870.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 However, a mass influx of investors into cryptocurrencies is likely to take more time. Ultimately, this move by \uc2 PayPal\uc2  proves that companies cannot ignore the rise of digital assets anymore.\par \par \uc2 Although the news is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a vertical rally may not materialize immediately. After the initial buying frenzy dies down, the extent of any future correction will confirm whether a new roaring bull market has begun or if institutional investors used this news to lighten up their positions in order to buy at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies and spot the critical levels to watch out for.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) soared above the resistance line of the ascending channel on Oct. 20. That was followed by a sharp up-move today when the bulls propelled the price above the stiff overhead resistance at $12,460.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5efe5c20-e842-4951-8a70-40b589ccc80f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A new 52-week high is generally a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign. The breakout of the ascending channel gives the BTC/USD pair a target objective of $12,975. If this level is crossed, the rally may extend to $14,000.\par \par \uc2 The current up-move has pushed the relative strength index to 80. Previous instances show that the risk of a correction increases when the RSI rises above 80.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close (UTC time) below the previous resistance turned support at $12,000.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can arrest the next correction at $12,000, it will signal strength and increase the possibility of a resumption of the up-move.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has held above the 20-day exponential moving average ($370) for the past few days. The failure of the bears to break this support has attracted buying from the aggressive bulls who are trying to sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $395.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/9fe4f6d8-9894-44a9-92b8-28994569be96.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will complete an ascending triangle pattern that has a target objective of $478. The gradually upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI above 61 suggest a marginal advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to throw in the towel so easily. They will attempt to defend the overhead resistance at $395. If the ETH/USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the uptrend line, it will signal weakness.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  is currently range-bound between $0.26 and $0.2295. After failing to sustain above the moving averages for the past two days, the altcoin has made a decisive move higher today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/a469b931-a501-418a-89dc-63c01fa2c6eb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the momentum and push the price above $0.26, the XRP/USD pair will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern. This setup has a target objective of $0.30.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls fail to push the price above $0.26, the bears will again try to sink the price below the moving averages. If they succeed, the pair may extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) broke down and closed (UTC time) below the critical support at $242 on Oct. 20 but the bears could not capitalize on this weakness.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/6e423812-7e32-40d5-a2ef-200c8962ba28.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BCH/USD pair has surged today, which shows strong buying by the bulls and short covering by the aggressive bears who may have opened short positions hoping for a fall to $200.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the momentum and push the price above $266.46, the pair could rally to $280 and then to $300. The bounce in the RSI from 50 shows strength.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bears sell the current rally and sink the pair below the $237.69.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed (UTC time) below the $29.5646 support and the 20-day EMA ($29) on Oct. 21. However, the bears could not capitalize on this advantage and intensify the selling.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/7a16a5c5-9576-4f6b-9f22-fafcb4fb1c39.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to push the price back above the downtrend line. If the BNB/USD pair closes (UTC time) above the downtrend line, a rally to $31.9798 and then to $33.3888 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current levels, the bears will once again attempt to sink the pair below the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the pair could decline to the 50-day simple moving average ($27).\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $11.199 on Oct. 19 and plunged below the moving averages on Oct. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/82ad7adb-6b40-445d-b018-365cbb204d6d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are not willing to surrender without a fight. They are currently attempting to push the price above the $11.199\u8211\'20\'13$11.8029 overhead resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed and the LINK/USD pair closes (UTC time) above the resistance zone, it will complete an ascending triangle pattern that has a target objective of $15.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the pair once again turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears will try to sink the price below the uptrend line. If that happens, a decline to $8.3817 is possible.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to push Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($4.14) and the bears are finding it difficult to sink the price below $3.80. This has kept the altcoin stuck inside a tight range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e1ee37e8-8910-4fa2-914b-5f882d254055.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Usually, a squeeze is followed by expansion. If the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USD pair could move up to $4.6112 and that could be followed by a rally to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has risen sharply to the midpoint. This suggests that the selling pressure has reduced.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price once again turns down from the overhead resistance and slips below $3.80, a retest of the $3.5321 is possible.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) price soared today and has reached the critical $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 overhead resistance zone. If the altcoin can close (UTC time) above this zone, it will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e8153d2c-147f-4b62-b1f1-3094cedf58f1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal pattern has a target objective of $61. The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI has risen above 63, which suggests an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears will pose a stiff challenge in the resistance zone. If the pullback from the current level is shallow, it will suggest that traders are not booking profits at the resistance and this will increase the possibility of the start of a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current levels and the bulls fail to arrest the decline above $50, the LTC/USD pair may again drop down to the moving averages.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have once again purchased the dip to the support line of the rising wedge pattern. They will now try to push Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) to the resistance line of the wedge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/72ffe5e0-0b79-4b6b-882d-6ff9e1220874.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, it is unlikely to be an easy task because the flat 20-day EMA ($0.10) and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. The bears will try to stall the recovery at the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears will make one more attempt to drag the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair below the wedge.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, a move to the resistance line of the wedge is possible. A breakout of the wedge could start a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) largely remains range-bound between $180.63 and $146.20. The bulls are currently attempting to sustain the price above the moving averages. If they can do that the altcoin could move up to the downtrend line and then to $180.63.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/f766ba52-301f-4017-85b2-d68cfe43dba0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the downtrend line, the bears will try to sink the BSV/USD pair to $146.20.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the flattish moving averages and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 The next trending move could start after the bulls push the price above $180.63 or the bears break the support at $146.20. Until then, volatile range-bound action is likely to continue.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5ldS1jZW50cmFsLTEuYW1hem9uYXdzLmNvbS9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvZjdlNjFiZjktYzlkNi00YzNiLTg0N2MtMDk1M2JkMGRmZGFiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201021egal000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/19: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LTC, BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price may rise to a new 52-week high if it can break above the ascending channel and this move could ignite the altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Crypto market sentiment appears to be improving across the board and the global push to mainstream central bank digital currencies is also making headway.\par \par \uc2 In China\u8217\'20\'19s Shenzhen province about 2 million people had applied for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/95-of-winners-in-china-s-cbdc-lottery-spent-digital-yuan-prizes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 digital yuan giveaway}}}\uc2  and the lucky 50,000 among them received \u8220\'20\'1Cred envelopes\u8221\'20\'1D of digital yuan totalling $1.5 million.\par \par \uc2 By the end of Oct. 18 about 47,573 of the recipients had spent roughly $1.3 million of the bounty, amounting to 88% of the total giveaway. This suggests that the pilot program was a success and shows that China is far ahead of other developed economies in developing their central bank digital currency..\par \par \uc2 To speed up the process of launching its CBDC, the Bank of Canada recently listed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/with-job-listing-canada-s-central-bank-takes-additional-steps-towards-a-cbdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 job opening}}}\uc2  for an economist with thorough knowledge of financial technology and digital currencies.\par \par \uc2 However, U.S. Federal Reserve Chair Jerome Powell seems unfazed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/better-to-get-it-right-than-to-be-first-with-cbdc-says-us-fed-chair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progress}}}\uc2  other countries are making with CBDCs. According to Powell, \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s more important for the United States to get it right than it is to be first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/1cf27d7b-fa2a-465e-be5a-053e61f5fc50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In other news, a survey by Statista shows that only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/still-so-early-7-of-americans-have-bought-bitcoin-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7% of Americans}}}\uc2  have used or owned Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 This figure is far less than Nigeria where the penetration rate is 32%, but also higher than Germany and Japan. This shows that the asset class has a long way to go before it can truly become a \u8216\'20\'18mainstream\u8217\'20\'19 currency.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment that dominated the markets for the past month appears to be alleviating as Bitcoin price moves closer the the $12K level.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to spot the ones that may perform well in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/70a7e900-a235-446d-b5b3-5676d133f888.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has risen to the resistance line of the ascending channel where it could face selling pressure from the bears. However, the upsloping 20-day exponential moving average ($11,201) and the relative strength index above 67 suggests that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can exploit this advantage and push the price above the channel, the up-move could pick up momentum and quickly rally to $12,048.05. A breakout of this level may challenge the yearly highs at $12,460.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up without a fight. They will try to stall the rally at the resistance line. If the price turns down from the current levels but stays above $11,500, then the BTC/USD pair could slowly grind higher inside the channel.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break below $11,178, and the trend will turn in favor of the bears if they can sink the price below the support line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears could not sustain Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) below the moving averages on Oct. 16 and 17. This attracted buying and the bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $395.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/7ec5b285-8ce1-4583-95d2-85396f9a10d5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($368) has started to turn up slowly, and the RSI has risen above 57, which suggests that bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push and close (UTC time) the price above $395, it will complete an ascending triangle pattern. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a target objective of $478, just below the 52-week highs at $488.134.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels or from $395 and plunges below the uptrend line. Such a move could keep the pair range-bound between $308.392 and $395 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 Although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  broke below the moving averages on Oct. 15, the bears could not capitalize on this advantage and sink the price to the bottom of the range at $0.2295. This suggests a lack of sellers at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/3bd071b9-531e-4f41-8910-fdf08bdf4587.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls have currently propelled the price back above the moving averages. If they can sustain the higher levels, there will be another attempt to clear the $0.26 hurdle.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above $0.26 is likely to start a new uptrend that may reach $0.2905 and then $0.303746.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the XRP/USD pair turns down from the current levels or $0.26, the range-bound action could continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have held the critical support at $242 for the past two days, and Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) is now attempting to resume its up-move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/95519268-3051-4cac-86f1-5f1c0f64635d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($241) and the RSI above 58 indicates that the bulls are in control. The first target on the upside is $266.46, and if that is scaled, the up-move can reach $280.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls fail to push the price above $266.46, the BCH/USD pair could remain range-bound for a few days. A break and close (UTC time) below the moving averages will indicate weakness and could pull the price down to $200.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The support at $29.5646 is acting as a new floor for Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ). Both moving averages continue to rise, and the RSI has been sustaining in the positive zone for the past few days, which suggests that bulls are in command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5a581bb3-db1b-4479-b573-9138fd7bd69e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now again try to push the price above the $32\u8211\'20\'13 $33.3888 resistance zone. If they can pull it off, the pair is likely to pick up momentum and challenge the all-time highs at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be negated if the BNB/USD pair turns down from the current levels or from the overhead resistance and sustains below the 20-day EMA ($29.17). Such a move could drag the price down to the 50-day simple moving average ($26.83).\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has held above the 20-day EMA ($10.52) for the past three days but the bulls have not been able to push the price back above the $11.1990\u8211\'20\'13$11.8028 resistance. This suggests that demand is drying up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/171d1d91-7042-44ad-841d-95877192af24.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the gradually upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory suggests a minor advantage to the bulls. The momentum could pick up after the bulls push the price above the overhead resistance zone. The first target is $13.28 and then $18.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the LINK/USD pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and breaks below $10.15. Such a move could pull the price down to the $8.7975 support.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sink Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) to $3.5321 suggests that lower levels are attracting buying by the bulls. If the buyers can push the price above the downtrend line, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  descending triangle setup will be invalidated.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/ad3e6060-4357-4947-9adc-230f0c13f381.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Above the downtrend line, the DOT/USD pair could move up to $4.6112 and if this level is crossed, the rally may extend to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up without a fight. The sellers will try to reverse the direction from the current levels and again at $4.6112. If the pair turns down from either resistance, it could again drop to $3.5321.\par \par \uc2 A breakdown and close (UTC time) below $3.5321 will signal that bears are back in command.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the 20-day EMA ($0.103), which shows that the sentiment is positive and the bulls are accumulating at lower levels. The buyers will once again try to push the price above the resistance line of the rising wedge pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/9d64785b-d2cf-45ff-90d9-c088c9142442.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can manage a close (UTC time) above the resistance line, a rally to $0.128062 and then to $0.1445 is possible. The upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI above 61 suggest that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from the resistance line, the bears will once again try to sink the price below the 20-day EMA and the support line of the wedge. If they can do that, the advantage will tilt in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the uptrend line and the bulls will now try to push the price above the moving averages. If the buyers can sustain the price above the moving averages, a move to the overhead resistance zone of $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/3ff86d7b-bdb8-432d-adc8-42fbb1b7559e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are unlikely to have it easy as the bears will try to defend the moving averages. If the LTC/USD pair turns down and breaks below the uptrend line, a drop to $42 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the flat 20-day EMA ($47.99) and the RSI at the midpoint suggests a balance between supply and demand. Hence, the price action could remain volatile for the next few days as both the bulls and the bears try to dominate proceedings.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above the resistance zone will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern that may signal the start of a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) is attempting to stage a recovery but the rebound off the Oct. 16 intraday lows lacks strength. This suggests that the bulls are in no hurry to buy as they are not confident that the bottom is in place.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/f6795268-4869-4560-a6cf-628c3aa00fbe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative zone suggest that the advantage is with the bears. If the bulls do not push the price above the moving averages within the next few days, the bears will make one more attempt to sink the price to $146.20.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above the moving averages, the BSV/USD pair could move up to $180.63. A breakout and close (UTC time) above this resistance could start a journey to $189 and then to $227.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5ldS1jZW50cmFsLTEuYW1hem9uYXdzLmNvbS9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvNTA4Y2VjYTItNzJhYy00MWIwLWE1NzEtMjgyZmZmYTdiODc2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201019egaj000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/16: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LTC, BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,764 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and the altcoins must rebound off their immediate support levels to recapture \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum and resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Chicago Mercantile Exchange\u8217\'20\'19s cash-settled Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) futures trading products \u8220\'20\'1Ccontribute more to price discovery than its related spot markets,\u8221\'20\'1D according to findings in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-futures-have-more-impact-on-price-than-spot-markets-says-wilshire-phoenix"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report by investment firm Wilshire Phoenix}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The increasing volumes of crypto derivative products highlight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/surging-bitcoin-futures-volume-highlights-increasing-institutional-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greater participation}}}\uc2  from institutional investors and this will likely be positive for the entire crypto space.\par \par \uc2 This is not unique to cryptocurrencies because even in most other asset classes, the derivatives markets lead the spot markets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/06181375-9d1d-420a-b333-837b581b4b4f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In a separate attempt to determine the valuation of Bitcoin, several experts from \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  opined that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/jpmorgan-says-bitcoin-slightly-overvalued-as-a-commodity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overvalued compared to its intrinsic value}}}\uc2  and the analysts suggested that BTC could face selling in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 The analysts consider Bitcoin to be a commodity and have calculated its marginal cost of production to estimate its intrinsic value.\par \par \uc2 While fundamentals do work in the long-term, short-term price action is usually dictated by sentiment and technicals. Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to determine the path of least resistance.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $11,178 support on Oct. 15 but the bulls could not sustain the price above $11,500. This weakness could have attracted profit booking by the short-term traders and shorting by the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e7932dc4-cf97-4b73-837e-1f7288668868.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to sink the price back below the critical support at $11,178. However, this level is likely to attract buyers because the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,081) is placed just below this support.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index in the positive territory suggest that buyers have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, it will be the first sign of strength. The uptrend could pick up momentum after the bulls can sustain the BTC/USD pair above the ascending channel.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the pair below the 20-day EMA, a drop to the support line of the channel is possible. A breakdown of the channel could spark further selling, which could result in a drop to $10,000.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to sustain Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) below the moving averages. If they succeed, a drop to the uptrend line is possible. If this support also cracks, it will indicate a range-bound action for the biggest altcoin for a few more days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/d4aa85ce-d1a4-4f13-a82f-361aaf96d16b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI near 50 also point to a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the ETH/USD pair turns up from the current levels or the uptrend line, the bulls will again try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $395. If they can pull it off, it will complete an ascending triangle pattern that has a target objective of $481.608.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  broke below the moving averages on Oct. 15 and is on its way to the critical support at $0.2295. Although the altcoin had formed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern, the bulls could not push the price above the neckline at $0.26 and the setup did not complete.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/0d828747-ce4f-44eb-b179-d32eb7b4c0b9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current price action of the altcoin is a good example of why traders should wait for the setup to complete before taking a directional bet. Buying in anticipation could quickly turn the trade into a loss.\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USD pair is currently range-bound between $0.2295 and $0.26, hence, the bulls are likely to buy near the support of the range.\par \par \uc2 A trending move will start after the bulls push the price above $0.26 or the bears sink the pair below $0.219712.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) witnessed sharp selling at $266.46 that resulted in a retest of the breakout level at $242. The sharp rebound off this support suggests that the bulls aggressively accumulated at lower levels and $242 has now flipped from resistance to support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/0fbf59af-7a08-4a86-bb3a-dd4b9c3ea9b4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($238) and the RSI above 60 suggests that the bulls have the upper hand. If the buyers can push the price above $266.46, the uptrend could reach $280 and then $300.\par \par \uc2 This assumption will be invalidated if the bears sell at the current levels and sink the BCH/USD pair below the moving averages. If that happens, the pair could again drop to $215.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has turned around from $31.9798 today as the bears attempt to stall the uptrend and sink the price back below the support at $29.5646 and the 20-day EMA at $28.77.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/8f6d1011-44be-431d-bd04-a9dd9150416e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the sellers can manage to sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened. A break below $26 could suggest the start of a deeper correction to $22.\par \par \uc2 However, if the BNB/USD pair rises from the $22.5646 support or the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 A strong rebound will suggest that the bulls are aggressively accumulating on dips, while a weak rebound will indicate a lack of demand, hence, the bears could pounce on it.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, traders can keep an eye on the strength of the rebound to determine whether the up-move will resume or the rally will fizzle out at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day simple moving average ($11.22) on Oct. 13 but the positive thing is that the bulls are attempting to arrest the pullback at the 20-day EMA ($10.40).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/0ba796ce-039e-45e5-a22a-e943512a9845.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A strong rebound off the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the sentiment has turned from sell on rallies to buy on dips. The first target is $12 and above this, the LINK/USD pair could reach $13.28.\par \par \uc2 However, if the rebound off the 20-day EMA is weak, it may again face stiff resistance at the 50-day SMA. If the pair once again turns down from this overhead resistance, it will increase the possibility of a decline to $8.7975.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has turned down from the 20-day EMA ($4.22) and the bears will now try to sink the price below the $3.5321 support. If the bears manage a close (UTC time) below $3.5321, it will complete a descending triangle pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/2393e002-4d11-4ac3-a235-dd8817d2e239.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a target objective of $1.4743. However, it may not be a straight fall to this level because the bulls could step in and provide support at $2.60 and again at $2.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the DOT/USD pair turns up from the current levels or rebounds off $3.5321, the bulls will try to push the price above the resistance line of the descending triangle.\par \par \uc2 If that happens, it will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern and that could result in an up-move to $4.6112 and then $5.5899.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not drive Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the neckline of the possible inverse head and shoulders pattern. This could have attracted profit booking by the short-term bulls and selling by the aggressive bears resulting in a drop to the 20-day EMA ($0.10).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/dadddea2-806e-4f0b-9664-d33886aa6e5a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 As the 20-day EMA is sloping up marginally and the RSI is in the positive zone, the bulls may defend this support. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will try to push the price above the neckline.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the pair could start a new uptrend that may reach $0.128062 and above it $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair continues to slip and it breaks below the 50-day SMA ($0.098). Such a move could result in a drop to $0.090.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has dropped below both moving averages today, which suggests that the bears used the rally to the $51 resistance to initiate short positions. However, the bulls have not yet given up as they are currently attempting to defend the uptrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5f030cc6-822e-42b1-8b1a-17357e95c648.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price above the moving averages, the selling is likely to intensify and the bears will once more try to sink the LTC/USD pair below the uptrend line. If they succeed, a drop to $42 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rises above the moving averages, the bulls will try to thrust the price above the $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 resistance zone. If they succeed, the inverse head and shoulders pattern will complete and it has a target objective of $60.3702.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the moving averages and is now likely to remain range-bound between $180.63 and $146.20. The fall today has invalidated the possibility of an inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/f8406e8a-c37f-405f-bd8b-e449fa3519a7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($166) is flat but the 50-day SMA ($167) is sloping down and RSI has dropped below 42, which suggests a slight advantage to the bears. A break below $146.20 could start a new downtrend.\par \par \uc2 However, if the BSV/USD pair recovers from the current levels or from the $146.20 support, the bulls will make one more attempt to drive the price above $180.63. A close (UTC time) above this resistance could start an up-move to $210.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5ldS1jZW50cmFsLTEuYW1hem9uYXdzLmNvbS9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvZTk3MTM5M2EtYzc5My00YzIwLTk4NGYtMWZkODUzM2QxNzY5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201016egag000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/14: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LTC, BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,773 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and most major altcoins are sustaining above their immediate support levels, increasing the possibility that the uptrend will resume\par \par \uc2 The bond yields across most developed economies have dropped sharply since the central banks unleashed a slew of measures to counter the economic crisis caused by the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 This could pose a challenge to the institutional investors who rely on the traditional 60/40 portfolio allocation between equities and fixed income instruments.\par \par \uc2 This week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fidelity-makes-it-clear-bitcoin-volatility-is-worth-the-risk-for-institutions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fidelity Digital Assets also released its Bitcoin Investment Thesis report}}}\uc2  which details how a portfolio with a Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) allocation as low as one to three percent can beat the traditional allocation on various time scales.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/415faca632ca49e98a7b7253219ccc6e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The report also highlights how Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s market capitalization could soar, even if it manages to attract a small portion of the alternative investment market which is currently valued at $13.4 trillion or the bond market which is worth over $50.3 trillion.\par \par \uc2 As of today, about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/public-companies-hold-almost-7b-in-bitcoin-in-heads-up-to-grayscale"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 public companies have allocated nearly $6.8 billion in Bitcoin investments}}}\uc2  this year, according to data from Coin98 Analytics. Although the total amount invested by the companies is only about 3.2% of the current market capitalization of Bitcoin, the encouraging sign is that the investments have been rising consistently.\par \par \uc2 If this trend continues and more institutional-sized investors enter the crypto space, Bitcoin price could rise quickly.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out what the dominant trend is in the markets.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $11,500 resistance and rallied to $11,719 on Oct. 12 but the bulls could not sustain the breakout. This shows that the higher levels are attracting selling by the short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/65cb4997f992d63ece49e564f80b40e8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair is correcting for the past two days but the positive thing is that the bulls have managed to keep the pair above $11,178.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day exponential moving average ($10,999) and the relative strength index above 60 suggests that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If buyers can push and sustain the price above 11,560, the pair could pick up momentum and resume its uptrend. The first target on the upside is $12,048 and if this level is scaled, the up-move may reach $12,460.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair weakens further from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA. Such a move will suggest that the momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are defending the $395 resistance to keep Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) range-bound between $395\u8211\'20\'13$308. However, the gradually rising 20-day EMA ($363) and the RSI in the positive territory suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/bd0b797f49808d8d4ca8d1e508447835.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls buy the dips to the moving averages, the ETH/USD pair may make one more attempt to rise above $395. If they succeed, the pair could start a rally that may reach the recent highs at $488.134.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the moving averages, the pair could drop to the uptrend line. If the pair rebounds off this support, the bulls will make one more attempt to drive the price above $395.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, if the price slips below the uptrend line, it could keep the pair range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not thrust {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above $0.26, hence, the inverse head and shoulders pattern did not complete. The moving averages have flattened out and the RSI has dropped to the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0aaae9ccb7cd17a35a3662721ad87ec2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink and sustain the price below the moving averages, the altcoin could consolidate for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the XRP/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($0.248), the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 If they manage to close (UTC time) the pair above $0.26, the inverse head and shoulders pattern will complete. This could start a rally that could climb up to $0.303746.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sink Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) back below the 20-day EMA ($234) on Oct. 12 showed a lack of selling pressure at lower levels. Traders viewed this as a buying opportunity and propelled the price above the overhead resistance at $242 on Oct. 13.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7e67637c61993dee2c549127d3871e02.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are about to complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI has risen above 68, which suggests that the bulls are in control. They will now try to push the BCH/USD pair to $280 and above it to $300.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up easily. They will make one more attempt to drag the price back below $242 and the 20-day EMA. If they can pull it off, it will indicate that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) soared above the overhead resistance on Oct. 12 but the bulls could not build upon the momentum and that resulted in the formation of a doji candlestick pattern on Oct. 13.\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the altcoin is taking a break as the bulls and the bears are uncertain about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2bcaab08849cec650da186ae6e58a041.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 64 suggest that the bulls are in command. If the bears fail to sink the price below $29.5646, the bulls will again try to drive the price to $33.3888.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($28.30), it will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened and a correction to the 50-day simple moving average ($26.07) could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are mounting a stiff resistance at the 50-day SMA ($11.38) for the past two days but the positive thing is that the bulls have not allowed Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) to drop below the 20-day EMA ($10.32).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/40f03af6c71ec1525fe12c1e5e8ebbfc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to move up gradually and the RSI in the positive territory suggests that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls drive the price above the 50-day SMA, the LINK/USD pair could rally to $13.28 and if this resistance also gets taken out, the up-move can reach $18.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair turns down from the current levels and plummets below the 20-day EMA, it will indicate weakness.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) had been clinging to the 20-day EMA ($4.25) for the past few days but the bears are currently attempting to resolve this indecision to the downside. The flat 20-day EMA and the RSI at the midpoint suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/248568ef79e653d8e78353256411eb98.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears can sink the price below $4, the DOT/USD pair could retest the critical support at $3.5321.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rebounds off $4, the bulls will take another aim at the overhead resistance at $4.6112. If the buyers manage to sustain the price above this level, a rally to $5.5899 is possible.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been facing resistance at the neckline of the possible inverse head and shoulders pattern for the past four days. The failure to break above the neckline has attracted selling and the bears will now try to sink the altcoin back below $0.104044.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/dc848cdbd6b586c16c1ae45ceb2a2dd3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair drops below the 20-day EMA ($0.100), it will signal that bears are shorting on rallies. They will then try to pull the price down to the right shoulder at $0.090.\par \par \uc2 However, the moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that bulls have the upper hand. If the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to push the price above the neckline.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will complete the reversal set up and start a new uptrend that may reach $0.128 and then $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are aggressively defending the $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 resistance zone but they have not been able to sink \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) below the immediate support at the 20-day EMA ($47.98).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8c462aeabdf88a7ffff2fc1724ba1fdf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the bulls are not closing their positions in a hurry. The moving averages on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI in the positive territory also indicate an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 A tight consolidation near a resistance is usually resolved to the upside. In this case, if the bulls can thrust the price above the resistance zone, a new uptrend could begin that may reach $64.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bears sink the LTC/USD pair below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) has been trading just above the 20-day EMA ($166) for the past two days with the bears trying to break the support and bulls attempting to defend it. The indicators are indecisive and are not giving a clear advantage to either the bulls or the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/f6800510eb3ef9e1bc09537ef615bae5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $155 is possible. A breakdown of this support may retest the critical support at $146.20.\par \par \uc2 If the BSV/USD pair rebounds off the current levels and rises above $180.63, it will complete an inverse head and shoulder pattern. Such a move could result in a rally to its pattern target of $218.29.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy80Yjg0NTI4OWVmOTdmZDgzNjE2ZDdhYTU2ZTlkNDI5ZS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201014egae000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/12: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LTC, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,732 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s strength above the $11,500 multi-year resistance is also pulling many altcoin prices higher\par \par \uc2 U.S. equity markets are nearing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/10/11/stock-market-futures-open-to-close-news.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all-time highs}}}\uc2  on the hopes that Democrats and Republican will break their current stalemate and strike a deal to release another round of stimulus for American citizens and the small businesses they operate.\par \par \uc2 While these monetary and fiscal stimulus measures have been proven to boost stock market returns in the short-term, they also add to the massive debt burden facing the U.S. Printing more money from thin air cannot be a permanent solution to every problem and at some point the chickens will come home to roost.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7be0a75c7af064b0bb09044a978a6807.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In the future this debt will become unmanageable and could lead to an economic and currency crisis. Several investors anticipate this and are hedging their risks by loading up on gold and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 These factors project a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view for Bitcoin in the long-term. However, in the short-term, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/dollar-dip-meets-hash-rate-boom-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  is likely to remain high until the U.S. presidential elections are over.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to see whether traders are \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $11,482.44 on Oct. 10, but the bulls held the price above the immediate support at $11,178. This shows strength because the bulls did not wait for a deeper pullback to buy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/22b44e5783f0d83b3a7df3b5e28ca780.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $11,500. If the BTC/USD pair sustains this rise, a rally to $12,050 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index has risen above 67, which suggests bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 If the momentum picks up and the bulls drive the price above $12,050, the pair could retest $12,460. A breakout of this level may resume the uptrend towards $14,000.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from the current levels and plummets below $11,178, it could signal aggressive shorting by the bears at higher levels. A break below the moving averages will shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 50-day simple moving average ($370) on Oct. 10 but could not sustain the higher levels. The biggest altcoin formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Oct. 11 but the positive thing is that it closed (UTC time) above the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/be50402ae3dbaaf928233d686c4b4861.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty resolved to the upside today and the bulls are currently attempting to propel the price above the overhead resistance at $395. If the bulls can pull this off, the ETH/USD pair could rise to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($360) has started to turn up and the RSI has risen above 61. This suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from $395 and breaks below the 20-day EMA. Such a move could result in a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  is struggling to break out of the overhead resistance at $0.26. If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.247), the altcoin could drop to $0.24. Such a move will suggest that the range-bound action is likely to continue for a few more days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ebec1b07054d3c06ebeda15c9c6c60dd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the XRP/USD pair breaks out and closes (UTC time) above $0.26, it will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern that has a target objective of $0.300288.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view of a possible reversal will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $0.24.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) above the $242 resistance on Oct. 10 and 11, but the long wicks on the candlesticks show that the buyers could not sustain the higher levels. Consequently, the price re-entered the $200\u8211\'20\'13$242 range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/5fdd5dc58a4f5749ade13c4a37156915.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the sharp rebound off the 20-day EMA ($230) today and the long tail on the candlestick shows strong buying at lower levels. The gradually rising 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive zone also suggest an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the BCH/USD pair breaks out and closes (UTC time) above the overhead resistance, it could start its northward march towards $280.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be negated if the pair again turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has broken out of the symmetrical triangle and the overhead resistance at $29.5646. This shows that the triangle acted as a continuation pattern and the bulls have come out on top.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1dc98f7ab4818b413172c7b0b7dc0275.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages continue to slope up and the RSI above 65 suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 The uptrend is likely to resume with the next possible stop at $33.3888 where the bears might again mount stiff resistance. However, if the bulls can drive the price above this resistance, the BNB/USD pair may retest the highs at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 50-day simple moving average ($25.72).\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) broke above the downtrend line on Oct. 11 and is now attempting to rise above the 50-day SMA ($11.53). If the bulls can sustain the price above $11.20, it will break the sequence of lower highs and lower lows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d3a6d1264d53532d8394a84cca488b06.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Such a move will suggest that the downtrend is over and the LINK/USD pair could either start a new uptrend or remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Above the 50-day SMA, the pair might move up to $13.28 where the bears are again likely to offer stiff resistance. However, if the bulls can push the price above $13.28, it could start a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from the current levels, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to rise above $4.6112. This suggests that the bears could be shorting on relief rallies to this resistance level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2fac125979f316d26ad9e8bef6e1e8d1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($4.28) is flat and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 This balance will tilt in favor of the bulls if they can push and sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $4.6112. Above this level, the DOT/USD pair could rally to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $4, it could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is facing resistance at the neckline of the possible inverse head and shoulders pattern but the positive thing is that the bulls did not allow the price to sustain below the immediate support at $0.104044.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/243a47f68388b9334cea644116ccd3b6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The buyers will again attempt to push the price above the neckline and if they succeed, it will complete the reversal pattern. The first target on the upside is $0.128 and if this level is scaled, the next stop could be $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the moving averages. Below this support, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair may drop to $0.09 and then to $0.0855.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 50-day SMA ($49.67) on Oct. 12 and the bulls will now try to push it above the overhead resistance zone of $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36. If they manage to do that the altcoin could start a new uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/c9d462a4df60ee7223c1c6f31e6609ab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($47.65) and the RSI above 62 suggests that the bulls have the upper hand. On a close (UTC time) above $52.36, the LTC/USD pair may rally to $64 and then to $68.9008.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the pair turns down from the overhead resistance zone, a few days of range-bound action is possible. The first sign of weakness will be a breakdown and close (UTC time) below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) broke above the resistance line of the descending triangle pattern on Oct. 10 and this move invalidated the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/87d2770f975b334190624ecfac9f7698.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears have not yet thrown in the towel because they are trying to stall the relief rally at the 50-day SMA ($0.158).\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price above the 50-day SMA, the bears will make one more attempt to sink the CRO/USD pair below $0.144743. If they succeed, the pair could drop to the next support at $0.124129 and then to $0.11.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can propel the price above the 50-day SMA, it could open the gates for a rally to $0.171541.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9kM2IwZGQwM2Q3MDc5YjE2ZGFhOGI1ZDRiOGUzYzc0NC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201012egac000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Top 5 cryptocurrencies to watch this week: BTC, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XMR, ATOM\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,621 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price could achieve a new 2020 high if bulls hold the price above the key multi-year resistance at $11.5K\par \par \uc2 In the past three years the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  has shot down several applications for a Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) exchange-traded fund. This dashed hopes of many investors who believed Bitcoin price would rally higher if an EFT was approved.\par \par \uc2 Although investors no longer pin BTC\u8217\'20\'19s future on the existence of an ETF, regulators could eventually adjust their anti-crypto stance in the future.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Cointelegraph, SEC Commissioner Hester Peirce said that the regulator will have to become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/secs-conservative-approach-to-crypto-may-need-to-change-secs-peirce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accommodative to innovation}}}\uc2  as several people from both the crypto space and traditional financial institutions seek their guidance.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\u8217\'20\'19s latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bloomberg-biden-election-would-be-good-for-bitcoin-bad-for-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto newsletter}}}\uc2  predicts that a Bitcoin ETF could see the light of the day if Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden is elected as the next U.S. President. The author believes that a change in guard may bring regulatory clarity that could attract investments into digital assets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4054a7599626a669b2132b18b38d2f10.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto market data daily view}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-fpje2fq19a_1589129732773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 However, even if President Donald Trump is re-elected, Bloomberg expects Bitcoin to extend its uptrend through his second term as the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be buoyed by the rising debt-to-GDP, quantitative easing, and Bitcoin hash rate.\par \par \uc2 Even if Bitcoin only rallies at half the speed of its 1,400% gain from 2016 to 2020, it would rally to $80,000 by 2024.\par \par \uc2 The long-term forecasts are encouraging and so are the short-term charts. Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-5 cryptocurrencies that may outperform in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The breakout of the symmetrical triangle on Oct. 8 attracted buyers who pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $11,178 on Oct. 10. However, the bears have not yet given up completely as they sold the rally to $11,482.44 on Sep. 10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/87bd58a4d147a13cef2c51891fac107d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls used the dip to buy and did not allow the price to break below $11,178. This suggests that the sentiment has changed from sell on rallies to buy on dips.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index above 64 indicate that the advantage is currently with the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can push the price above the overhead resistance at $11,500, the next stop for the BTC/USD pair could be $12,000 and then $12,460.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day exponential moving average ($10,853). Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/00031f30c3636dd215dc43dc4b6ed5cd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The trend on the 4-hour chart has turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  with both moving averages sloping up and the RSI in the overbought territory. The buyers will again attempt to push the price above $11,500 and if they succeed momentum is likely to pick up.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, it could consolidate in a tight range of $11,468.98\u8211\'20\'13$11,178 for some time. A break below $11,178 will be a sign of short-term weakness.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears defended the $0.26 overhead resistance on Oct. 10, but they could not sustain the selling pressure today. This shows that the bulls are buying on every minor dip and are currently attempting to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above $0.26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b98f95095454bb3984a218530afaf371.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above $0.26 will complete an inverse head and shoulders setup that has a pattern target of $0.300288. The moving averages on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI close to 60 suggest advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the XRP/USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($0.246), it will show that the bears are aggressively shorting on rallies to $0.26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/af261e4dad7bbf7da7a2d7659c5cc2d7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are attempting to defend the $0.26 resistance but they have not been able to sink the price below the 20-EMA. This suggests that the bulls are accumulating on dips.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI near 60 suggest that bulls have the upper hand in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 A break below the 20-EMA will be the first sign of weakness and the advantage will turn in favor of the bears if they can sink the price below the $0.24 support.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above $0.26, a new uptrend is likely. The pair could face resistance at $0.266 and then at $0.28 but the trend will remain \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the price remains above the neckline.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sustain Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) below $0.90, between Oct. 7 to 9, attracted aggressive buying by the bulls who then pushed the price above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/394aaaf0e77b6ab8e60824abf7ee3170.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI near 62 suggest that the buyers have the upper hand. If they can propel the price above the neckline, it will complete a reversal setup that has a pattern target of $0.1331.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the moving averages. Such a move will suggest that the breakout above $0.104044 was a bull trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/eb96642f9acd1d92397a5d3520e7d48c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the immediate support at $0.1040440 suggests that the sentiment has turned positive as the bulls are viewing dips as a buying opportunity.\par \par \uc2 However, unless the bulls drive the price above the neckline, the bears will again try to sink the pair back below $0.1040440 and the 20-EMA. If they succeed, the pair could drop to the 50-simple moving average and below it to $0.90.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rebounds off the 20-EMA, it will indicate strength and increase the possibility of a break above the neckline.\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD\par \par \uc2 Monero ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xmr-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR}}}\uc2  ) is in an uptrend with both moving averages sloping up and the RSI in the overbought zone. The bulls will now try to extend the up-move to $140 and above it to $150.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/62786ea662087c2c19aaf3e87cb5e1f8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 In a strong uptrend, the corrections usually last for one to three days and the bulls view the dips to the 20-day EMA ($105.96) as a buying opportunity because it gives a low-risk entry point with a good risk to reward ratio.\par \par \uc2 However, if the XMR/USD pair turns down from the current levels and drops back below $121.427, the bears will try to drag the price to the 20-day EMA. A break below this support will be the first sign of weakness.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/3d2a02cbbc267f3e279bc785878a23c2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The ascending triangle pattern completed on a breakout and close (UTC time) above $113.211. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a pattern target of $132.739. The buyers are currently attempting to sustain the price above $121.427.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will suggest that $121.427 will now act as a strong support. Even if the price dips back below this level, the bulls will again try to buy the dip to the 20-EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the pair rebounds off this support, it will indicate strength and increase the possibility of a resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD\par \par \uc2 Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed (UTC time) above the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders pattern on Oct. 10. This breakout has seen further buying today and the bulls have pushed the price above the $5.877 resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e1013016e4734ad76568450244f6968d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ATOMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The ATOM/USD pair could now start a rally that may reach $7.40 and then $8.877. The 20-day EMA ($5.17) has started to turn up and the RSI has risen into the positive territory, which suggests a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from the current levels, the bears will try to sink the price back below the neckline and the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If that happens, it will indicate that the current breakout was a fake one. The trend will turn in favor of the bears if the pair drops below the right shoulder at $4.549.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7740b24940c4fec0d849443f1647d63a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ATOMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $5.877 that could start a new uptrend. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI is in the positive territory suggest advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bulls fail to defend the breakout level during the next retest. If the price becomes pinned below the neckline this will be a sign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy8zYWQzNGE4MWRkMTkwZTdmYzcwZDE4MzBjMDU5YTNiNS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201011egab000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 $12K Bitcoin price back on the table after BTC rallies above $11.4K\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ray Salmond \par \uc2 440 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price rallied to $11,491 after bulls managed to flip the $11K level from resistance to support\par \par \uc2 On Friday Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/coin/bitcoin-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price finally managed to break above the symmetrical triangle where the price had been compressing for the last 30 days. After holding the $11,000 level into the daily close, the price rallied to $11,448 on multiple high volume surges.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/37ee3dabdb0f40d07689019ed84ea4a2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrency daily market performance snapshot}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency daily market performance snapshot. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-c9jl7xfl0t_1602306957271"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 On Oct. 8 Cointelegraph contributor Micheal van de Poppe explained that in his view:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the price of Bitcoin breaks through the $11,100-$11,300 resistance zone, further bullishness can be expected towards $12,000. This makes the $11,100-$11,300 area is a critical zone for continuation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Currently the price is holding above $11,400 and meeting resistance at $11,489 which is right at the top of the Sept. 3 candle which saw BTC drop 13% to $9,960. This level aligns with the VPVR node extending from $11,400-$11,740, but if the bulls are able to push through this resistance cluster another run at the $12K mark is on the cards.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b9f16ef5ea0812ddfc1d9aafdbd79a0d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 On the daily timeframe, the relative strength index has risen to 65, a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal, and the MACD histogram clearly reflects the current bump in momentum.\par \par \uc2 As is always the case, day traders should keep a close eye on volume as the lack of it during the last 30-days is the primary reason for Bitcoin price being flat and pinned below $11,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2e0133ea8ed2c65a7b6ed36a2ca03f15.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price daily performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price daily performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/coin/bitcoin-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/ethereum/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) price also took a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  turn, by piercing a key descending trendline to rally 3.08% to $378.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/266963f96b7e3a38271e2d80bf246964.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ether/USDT daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 At the time of writing the top altcoin is encountering resistance at $375 where there is a high volume VPVR node extending from $376-$389. If bulls are able to maintain the current momentum and push through this resistance zone, Ether price could run to $419.\par \par \uc2 As BTC and Ether rallied, the majority of altcoins followed suit with double-digit gains. Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/cardano/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) gained 10.19%, Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/chainlink/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) added 11.4% and Aave ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/aave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEND}}}\uc2  ) rallied by 15%.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinMarketCap}}}\uc2 , the overall cryptocurrency market cap now stands at $361.5 billion and Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/charts/#dominance-percentage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominance index}}}\uc2  is currently at 58.4%.\par \par \uc2 Keep track of top crypto markets in real time {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/price-indexes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9mMjg4ODc0N2RkYmRmNThlMDk3MzYxNmU0ZDdkZjE4OS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201010egaa00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/5: BTC, ETH, XRP, BNB, BCH, DOT, LINK, CRO, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,938 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Traders are attempting to kickstart a new trending move in Bitcoin and altcoins by attacking overhead resistance levels\par \par \uc2 A recent report by \uc2 ARK Investment Management LLC\uc2  presents a strongly \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  case for Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) future value. The group projects that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s network capitalization will rise to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ark-invest.com/white-papers/bitcoin-part-two/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1-$5 trillion}}}\uc2  over the next five to ten years. The asset manager argues that Bitcoin offers one of the most attractive risk to reward ratios and should be included in well-diversified portfolios.\par \par \uc2 However, Blockstream CEO Adam Back believes that the estimation is \u8220\'20\'1Cconservative\u8221\'20\'1D and Back suggested that Bitcoin could rally to a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-pioneer-predicts-1t-btc-market-cap-by-2022-or-sooner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1 trillion market cap}}}\uc2  within 2 years\u8221\'20\'1D or probably sooner, implying that each Bitcoin will be worth $50,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1661a54c2cb3b1223c3b471ceb848eca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Other than buying and holding Bitcoin for the long-term, some aggressive traders add leverage through Bitcoin options as it allows them an opportunity to lock in greater gains with a fixed risk if proven correct.\par \par \uc2 As more institutional investors enter the crypto space, the liquidity in the options market is likely to increase further. The Bitcoin options {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-options-open-interest-sets-new-high-sparked-by-rising-liquidity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open interest has been increasing}}}\uc2  over the past few months, and it hit an all-time high of $2.14 billion on Sep. 24, which shows increasing participation from traders.\par \par \uc2 While analysts have painted a rosy long-term picture for Bitcoin, what does the short-term project? Can the crypto markets resume their up-move, or will higher levels attract selling by the bears?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is currently trading inside a symmetrical triangle, which suggests that both the bulls and the bears are not clear about the next directional move. The big question is when will the breakout happen and which direction will it take.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1f20e06e69c9bca4794abab8cac081e3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair has reached about three-fourths of the distance from the base of the triangle to the apex. Ideally, a breakout should happen within the next few days and both the bulls and the bears will attempt to dominate proceedings.\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day exponential moving average ($10,693) and the relative strength index close to the midpoint suggests that it could be anybody\u8217\'20\'19s game.\par \par \uc2 In a triangle, the price moves between the support line and the resistance line. After the bounce off the support line on Oct. 2, the bulls may attempt to push the price above the triangle. If they succeed, the pair could start an up-move with a target objective of $12,460.\par \par \uc2 However, if the breakout fails and the bears sink the price below the support line, then a drop to $9,835 would be on the cards. The next few days are critical as the pair could start a new trending move.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) had turned down from the downtrend line on Oct. 1 but the bears could not capitalize on the weakness and sink the price to the $308.392 support. The long tails on the candlesticks from the start of the month show accumulation by the bulls at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/478435ea8a05107dc85b9ce79e1b0c4a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now attempt to push the price above the downtrend line and if they prevail, a move to the 50-day simple moving average ($376) or even $395 is possible. A break above $395 may signal the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are unlikely to have an easy ride as the bears will mount stiff resistance at overhead resistance and the 50-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair turns down from the downtrend line, the bears will once again try to sink the price to $308.392. A break below this support may start a deeper correction to $240.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sink {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  below the $0.2295 support on Oct. 2 and 3 attracted aggressive buying from the short-term traders who pushed the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.242) and the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9ef6790d4a94b7e3e364baa44afb6668.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory show that the selling pressure has reduced. If the bulls can capitalize on this advantage and push the price above $0.26, the XRP/USD pair could rally to $0.303746.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up easily. They are currently attempting to stall the up-move at the 50-day SMA ($0.256). If they can sink the price back below the downtrend line, it will suggest that the current breakout was a bear trap.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) bounced sharply from just below the 20-day EMA ($26.94) on Oct. 2 and broke above the downtrend line on Oct. 4. However, the bulls seem to have hit a wall at the overhead resistance at $29.5646.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d1f3a5150eb9b47155570bddf1a3f2f3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently trying to pull the price back below the downtrend line and if they succeed, the BNB/USD pair could drop to the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 A sharp rebound from this support will confirm that the bulls are buying on dips, while a break below it will signal near-term weakness.\par \par \uc2 However, the rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the pair rebounds off the downtrend line, it will suggest strength and increase the possibility of a break above the overhead resistance at $29.5646.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the lows on Oct. 2 but they have not been able to sustain the buying at higher levels. This suggests that the bulls are hesitant to buy Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) near the stiff resistance of the 20-day EMA ($225) and the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8d0819988e3b2d5474891b6ad1be3631.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls do not push the price above the downtrend line within the next few days, the bears will again attempt to sink the BCH/USD pair to $210.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory suggest a slight advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls overcome the selling and propel the pair above the downtrend line, a rally to the 50-day SMA ($244) is possible. This level could act as a stiff resistance but once crossed, the pair may rise to $280.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the $3.90 support in Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) lacks strength, which shows that the bulls are in no hurry to buy at the current levels because they may not be confident that the correction has ended.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/f5c3c72356f5f2bba8dd9622ff9f6f0c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA ($4.41), the bears will make one more attempt to sink the DOT/USD pair below $3.90. If they succeed, a drop to $3.5321 and then to $2.782 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could move to $4.6112 and above it to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the bulls buy on dips to $3.90 and the bears defend the resistance at $4.6112. Currently, all options are open, hence, traders may wait for a trending move to start before placing large bets.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) is attempting a relief rally from $8.7975 but the rebound lacks strength, which shows low conviction among the buyers to accumulate at current levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a276984c66be9611d29b439712ca5cc1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the momentum does not pick up, the LINK/USD pair might again turn down from the 20-day EMA ($10.13). Such a move will suggest that bears continue to sell on minor rallies.\par \par \uc2 The sellers will then try to sink the price below $8.7975 and if that happens, a retest of $6.90 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 A breakout of the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the bears might be losing their grip and a break above the downtrend line could signal a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are defending the $0.144743 support but the rebound from the current levels could again face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA ($0.153) and then at the downtrend line. If Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) turns down from either level, the bears will again try to sink the price below $0.144743.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/07f7125c453650ae063d8251fd3005e5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A breakdown and close (UTC time) below $0.144743 will complete a descending triangle pattern that has a target objective of $0.10607. The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls can propel the CRO/USD pair above the resistance line of the triangle and the 50-day SMA ($0.160), the uptrend could resume. The first target objective is $0.171541 and above it $0.191101.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has again reached the 20-day EMA ($46.66) where it is facing stiff resistance from the bears. However, the positive thing is that unlike the previous occasions on Oct. 1 and 2, the altcoin has not witnessed a sell-off.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9d34ffb4a93390a9d746d4baaa96fca8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the LTC/USD pair does not lose ground, the possibility of a move to the downtrend line increases. The bears may try to stall the relief rally at the downtrend line but if the bulls can push the price above it, the pair could move up to $51.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI has risen above 46, which suggests that the selling pressure has reduced.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  assumption, if the pair again turns down from the current levels or the downtrend line, the bears will try to sink the price below $41.6298. If they succeed, the pair could drop to the critical support at $39.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is currently facing resistance at the downtrend line but the positive thing is that the bulls are attempting to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.095). If they succeed, the possibility of a breakout of the 50-day SMA ($0.103) increases.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/38848c936b5c9c123171e629c29775c6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has risen to the 50 level, which suggests that the bears are losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair has also formed an inverse head and shoulders pattern that will complete on a breakout and close above the neckline. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a target objective of $0.1331.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the $0.0898\u8211\'20\'13$0.0855 support zone.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9lMjUzM2RjOTU3NTBkOTlhZDNmZWJjYzk3NWU3NGZlYi5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201005ega5000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Top 5 cryptocurrencies to watch this week: BTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XMR, ATOM, VET\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,623 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin could consolidate for a few more days but select altcoins have formed reversal patterns that may lead to a trending move\par \par \uc2 Investors are concerned about the stability of the cryptocurrency market after it was faced with a flurry of adverse news in the past few days.\par \par \uc2 Fortunately, the markets have matured to the extent that negative news no longer provokes wild price swings like they once did in crypto\u8217\'20\'19s early days.\par \par \uc2 The current stability shows that institutional investors do not consider the recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-unfazed-after-150m-hack-of-major-exchange-kucoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KuCoin hack}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cftc-charges-bitmex-with-illegally-operating-derivatives-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CFTC and DOJ charges}}}\uc2  against BitMEX, or even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/three-key-reasons-dow-plunge-wont-cause-a-bigger-bitcoin-drop-below-10k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Donald Trump being diagnosed with coronavirus}}}\uc2  as serious enough events to crash the crypto markets.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, there was no panic liquidation in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) futures after the news broke and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-bitmex-scandal-bitcoin-futures-data-shows-traders-focused-on-12k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open interest}}}\uc2  remained stable.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7d051424e6899911c2474e6d729bf991.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-fpje2fq19a_1589129732773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend, traders use price weakness caused by knee-jerk reactions to add to their positions. If Bitcoin continues to sustain above the psychologically critical level at $10,000, more investors may consider adding to their portfolios.\par \par \uc2 Despite Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s sideways price action, a few altcoins have maintained their uptrend and others are showing signs of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend reversal.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 5 cryptocurrencies to see which critical levels may signal the start of a trending move.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The long-term trend in Bitcoin is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the 200-day simple moving average ($9,448) is sloping up. However, in the short-term, the flat 20-day exponential moving average ($10,682) and the relative strength index close to the midpoint suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ba6750707bb7dd51150df7bf772a45f3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair is currently stuck between $9,835 and $11,178 for the past few days. A break above or below this range could start a trending move.\par \par \uc2 Between May and July, the pair had remained stuck in a tight range for almost 80 days and the current consolidation has completed about 30 days.\par \par \uc2 If history were to repeat itself, then the price may remain range-bound for a few more days. Hence, traders should be patient until the price breaks above or below the range.\par \par \uc2 A breakout of $11,178 could start a rally with the first target objective at $12,460, while a break below $9,835 and the 200-day SMA may intensify selling as traders rush to the exit to dump their positions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/186f6486c25e4a28e0fe7c7d20caa874.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the price is trading inside a large symmetrical triangle. A breakout between half to three-fourths of the distance from the base of the triangle to the apex is considered as reliable.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, the bulls and the bears might attempt a breakout of the triangle within the next few days. However, if that does not happen and the price reaches the apex of the triangle, then the pattern will be invalidated.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) closed (UTC time) below the 200-day SMA ($0.0837) on Sep. 23 but the bears could not sustain the lower levels, and the altcoin climbed back above the long-term moving average on Sep. 24.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7c3454bdf303bcfc051047d88a62090d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the bulls are aggressively defending the 200-day SMA. The price action of the past few days is showing a possible inverse head and shoulders pattern formation that will complete on a breakout and close (UTC time) above the neckline.\par \par \uc2 The pattern target of this setup is $0.1331. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will come into play only after the price breaks out of the neckline.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from the current level or the neckline and drops below the 200-day SMA, it will invalidate the pattern. This could attract aggressive selling with the next support at $0.050.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ca29a832b32102675c94880c292349d4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bulls are struggling to push the price above the $0.1040440 overhead resistance. This shows that the bears are selling on relief rallies to this resistance.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in negative territory suggest that bears have a slight advantage in the short-term. If the price dips below $0.0898, the bears will try to sink the price to the critical support at $0.074.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push and sustain the price above the moving averages, a move to $0.1040440 and then to the neckline is possible.\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD\par \par \uc2 Monero ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xmr-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $97.70 overhead resistance on Sep. 29 and the retest of the breakout level was successful on Oct. 2. This shows that the level that was previously acting as a stiff resistance is now acting as a strong support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2d98b5ecf9244b596c2db6ef4c373029.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($97.15) and the RSI in the positive territory suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside. The first target is $113.211 and above it $121.427.\par \par \uc2 Momentum is likely to pick up if the bulls can push the price above this level and the next target is at $140.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the XMR/USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $93. Such a move could pull down the price to the 200-day SMA at $71.79.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ce71ca13b8636b3470d600cb98f2994e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the pair has largely been trading inside a channel for the past few days. Although the price broke above the channel, the bulls could not sustain the higher levels and the pair dropped to the support line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 However, the rebound from the support line has been strong and the bulls are once again trying to push the price above the channel. If they succeed, the momentum could pick up.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price fails to breakout of the channel, then a gradual up-move is likely. The first sign of weakness will be a break below the channel.\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD\par \par \uc2 Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ) is showing signs of a possible reversal as it has formed an inverse head and shoulders pattern that will complete on a breakout and close (UTC time) above the neckline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4754bbbc1dd53e5a59596080c52919f6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ATOMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This setup has a target objective of $7.4 and if this level is crossed, the up-move can retest the highs at $8.877.\par \par \uc2 However, the 20-day EMA ($5) is currently flat and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand. Therefore, traders may wait for the price to break above the neckline before turning positive.\par \par \uc2 If the ATOM/USD pair turns down from the neckline, a drop to $4.50 and below it to the 200-day SMA ($3.675) is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/930ed535c831d26aabc9047b21346fba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM/USD 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ATOMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bulls purchased the dip to the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of the rise from $3.78\u8211\'20\'13$5.596. The buyers will now try to push the price back above $5.596.\par \par \uc2 If they achieve the breakout and sustain it, the inverse head and shoulders pattern will complete.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels or from the overhead resistance and drops below the 61.8% retracement level of $4.474. Such a move could drag the price down to $3.78.\par \par \uc2 VET/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have been defending the $0.01094 support for the past few days but they have failed to sustain the higher levels, which suggests that bears are selling on rallies. Hence, VeChain ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/vechain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 VET}}}\uc2  ) has again dropped back to the $0.01094 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1a6517a7e76d03e3fa562a9c99d4c8e0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 VET/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 VET/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/VETUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the VET/USD pair below $0.01094 support and the 200-day SMA ($0.0104), the selling is likely to intensify and a drop to $0.008 and below it to $0.0066 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.0128) is sloping down and the RSI has not been able to sustain above 50, which suggests that bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the pair again rebounds off the support and rises above $0.0160. Such a move will suggest accumulation by the bulls at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4f09d690f11536eccba950c6a90c0861.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 VET/USD 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 VET/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/VETUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows the formation of a descending triangle, which will complete on a breakdown and close (UTC time) below $0.010940. This setup has a target objective of $0.00328.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative zone suggest that bears have the upper hand in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the pair rebounds off $0.010940 and rises above the downtrend line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy8zZDc3YjBmNzlmZTU5YmIzNTc0MDdhZDFiYjlmNTA1Ny5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201004ega4000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/30: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, DOT, LINK, BSV, CRO,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and a few altcoins continue to push against resistance at higher levels, suggesting that the uptrend may resume soon\par \par \uc2 According to data from CryptoQuant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-exchange-reserves-down-5b-in-2020-hints-at-whale-accumulation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the total amount of Bitcoin (BTC) held in exchange reserves dropped from 2.8 million BTC in October 2019 to 2.4 million}}}\uc2 . Analysts believe that this steady decline in reserves means retail traders and whales may be accumulating Bitcoin as they expect prices to rise in the future.\par \par \uc2 Even though Bitcoin is still far below its lifetime highs, if it manages to close Q3 2020 above $10,590, that would be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/at-10-600-bitcoin-price-is-on-track-for-its-second-best-quarter-ever"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second-best close in any quarter}}}\uc2 . Data from Skew shows this would only be behind the Q4 2017 closing price at $13,660.\par \par \uc2 All of this suggests that the crypto markets are moving into the hands of stronger investors who are not perturbed daily price fluctuations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/874ad9a1a4cb85a4fc1d5bd7b1299509.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors are said to have deep pockets and favor holding long-term positions. Data from Bybit shows that Grayscale Investments currently holds 449,900 Bitcoin, which is over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-investments-now-controls-24-of-the-current-btc-supply"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2% of Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s maximum possible}}}\uc2  supply.\par \par \uc2 If institutional investors increase their allocations to cryptocurrencies, demand could eventually exceed supply and that could boost Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to analyze the path of least resistance for the top-10 cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been hovering around the 20-day exponential moving average ($10,732) for the past few days. Although the bulls had tried to break away on Sep. 29, they could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ed00743a2967011938ea92c1ea997078.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears have not been able to capitalize on the weakness and sink the price below the $10,500 support. This shows indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA and the relative strength index near the midpoint suggests a balance between supply and demand. It is difficult to predict the direction of the next breakout from this range.\par \par \uc2 However, sometimes, the movement of the RSI can provide some hints. If the RSI rises above the symmetrical triangle and the 55 level, it increases the possibility that the bulls may attempt a breakout of $11,178.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BTC/USD pair can rally to $12,000 and then to $12,460. Conversely, if the bears sink the price below $10,500 and the uptrend line, a drop to $9,835 is likely.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are attempting to stall the relief rally at the 20-day EMA ($361). If the price turns down and breaks below $337, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) could drop to $308.392.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/bafb4f8313875e19d8fd2bb88407546a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 When the price fails to rise above the 20-day EMA in a down move, it suggests that the sentiment is negative and the bears are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down marginally and the failure of the RSI to rise above the 50 level suggests that bears have the upper hand. A break below the critical $308.392 support could result in a fall to $240.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the ETH/USD pair turns up and breaks out of the 20-day EMA. Such a move could result in a rally to $395.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The pullback from the Sep. 24 intraday low of $0.219712 has hit a wall at the 20-day EMA ($0.243). The failure of the bulls to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the 20-day EMA suggests that the bears may be shorting at this resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8bac5428cdaa814c248cde7520f6caa3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down marginally and the RSI is just below the 50 level, which suggests that bears are at a slight advantage.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the XRP/USD pair below the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.219712 support zone, the downtrend may resume with the next stop at $0.19.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will be the first sign that the selling pressure is reducing. A breakout of $0.26 will suggest a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to sustain Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($227) for the past four days suggests a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/959139ba32ced187623fb8c54991c80c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $223, a drop to $210 and then to $200 will be on the cards. A break below the critical support of $200 will be a huge negative as it could signal the start of a possible downtrend.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be negated if the BCH/USD pair turns up and breaks out of the downtrend line and the overhead resistance at $242. Above this level, the up-move can reach $280.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The pullback in Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) reached the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $29.0886 on Sep. 29 where it is facing resistance. However, if the altcoin does not give up much ground, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $29.0886.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d1850472e249abfe7a9b2bb18ffe19a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BCH/USD pair could move up to the 78.6% Fibonacci retracement level of $30.9884 and above it to $33.4084. The rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to pull down the price but the bulls are likely to buy the next dip to the 20-day EMA aggressively as the trend is up. The failure to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($4.55) suggests weakness. Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has turned down and the bears will now try to sink the price below the $4\u8211\'20\'13$3.5321 support zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0ea0a929d603094f3a2c9bc46b2b94cb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could give up ground and drop to $2.782 and below it to $2. The gradually downsloping 20-day EMA and the failure of the RSI to sustain above 50 suggests that the bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair again rebounds off $4 or turns up from the current levels, the bears will attempt to push the price above the 20-day EMA. If they can accomplish that, the pair may move up to $4.921 and then to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($10.60) could have prompted profit booking from the short-term traders. The bears will now try to capitalize on this weakness and sink Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) below the immediate support at $9.3771.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1261932ce0374a59913395d4a6c9158e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the LINK/USD pair may drop to $6.90. The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has been sustaining below 50 for the past few days, which suggests that the bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off the $9.3771 support, a few days of range-bound action is possible. A break above $11.1990 will be the first sign that the selling pressure has reduced.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the downtrend line on Sep. 28 but the bulls did not allow the price to dip below the 20-day EMA ($166). The buyers have today pushed the price above the downtrend line and are attempting to scale it above the 50-day SMA ($180).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a90cf12797a03cabaebb098d984a4253.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is turning up gradually and the RSI has risen into the positive territory, which suggests that the bulls are at a slight advantage. If they can propel the BSV/USD pair above the 50-day SMA, it will increase the possibility of a rally to $208.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair turns down from the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that the bears are aggressively defending this level. The sellers will then attempt to sink the pair below the $146.20\u8211\'20\'13$135.00 support zone.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) has been trading below the moving averages for the past few days but the bears have failed to sink the price below the immediate support at $0.144743.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ae10005c03e176b71e5ae0d5e07b5f15.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the CRO/USD pair does not rise above the moving averages within the next few days, it could result in another round of selling that could challenge the $0.144743 support.\par \par \uc2 A break and close (UTC time) below this level will complete the descending triangle pattern, which has a target objective of $0.10607.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup will be invalidated if the bulls push the price above the downtrend line of the triangle. Above this level, a move to $0.183416 and then to $0.191101 is possible.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The strong relief rally in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) could not rise above the downtrend line on Sep. 28, but the positive sign is that the bulls have not allowed the price to dip below the 20-day EMA ($0.0955).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/be893b4123e424ae1d3ae9481ffb8380.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is sloping up and the RSI has been sustaining above 50, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will once again attempt to push the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, the pair could move up to $0.1280.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the pair below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $0.0855982 and then to $0.0755701 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy8xYjhhZmMwMDIxNzUxMjg1MTIwZGUxYmVjMmExZjI0ZS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200930eg9u000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/28: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, DOT, LINK,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins may hit a few roadblocks in the short-term as they near stiff overhead resistance levels, but the overall trajectory remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) soared above $10,000 on July 27 and has sustained above this level since then. Data shows that this streak of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-sets-record-for-most-days-above-10-000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 63 consecutive days}}}\uc2  of closes above the $10,000 level is a new record.\par \par \uc2 This also shows that the level has now become a strong support after previously acting as a stiff resistance. Bulls have consistently purchased dips to and below $10K and this psychologically important level may now act as a floor for launching the next leg of the uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b1976f79191cf9c3d223bb28fe4d4ddf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 At the moment it seems that the monetary and fiscal stimulus measures unleashed across the globe have increased the allure of cryptocurrencies as investors look for alternative investment opportunities to safeguard their portfolio from the debasing of fiat currencies.\par \par \uc2 With less than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/only-25-million-bitcoin-left-to-mine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2.5 million Bitcoin}}}\uc2  left to be mined, the scarcity factor could soon come into play as demand from institutional investors picks up.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of downside price action and short periods of consolidation, can Bitcoin and altcoins build upon the bullishness of the past few days to resume the uptrend?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is currently range-bound between the uptrend line and the overhead resistance at $11,178. The flat moving averages and the relative strength index just above the midpoint suggest a few days of consolidation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ead2525f0a8ee7793bf008f3ca176752.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears will mount a stiff resistance in the zone between the 50-day simple moving average ($11,097) and the downtrend line. If the price turns down from either resistance, the bears will try to sink the price below the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BTC/USD pair can drop to the critical support at $9,835. The selling could intensify if this critical support breaks down.\par \par \uc2 However, during the next dip, if the pair rebounds off the uptrend line, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance and resume the uptrend. The first target on the upside is $12,048 and above it $12,460.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has risen above the downtrend line and the bulls are now trying to push the price above the 20-day exponential moving average ($362). This up-move suggests that the selling pressure has reduced.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7a8eb78a91ac060adc9be3da521b24c1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair breaks and closes (UTC time) above the 20-day EMA, a quick rally to the 50-day SMA ($385) is possible.\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to defend the zone between the 50-day SMA and $395 and if the price turns down from this resistance, the pair could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, a breakout of $395 will signal the possible resumption of the uptrend with a target objective of $488.134.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and the bears sink the price below the critical support at $308.392.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to sustain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the 20-day EMA ($0.244). If they can accomplish this task, a move to $0.26 is possible. The bears will try to defend this resistance and the 50-day SMA ($0.263) placed just above it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/eff0e074396ad9caef87f4cbc7d07b84.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $0.26, the XRP/USD pair could remain range-bound for a few more days. The longer the time spent in consolidation, the stronger will be the eventual breakout from it.\par \par \uc2 A break above the 50-day SMA could result in a rally to $0.303746 and if this is crossed, the pair may move up to $0.326113. The trend could turn negative if the bears sink the price below the recent lows at $0.219712.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The strong bounce in Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has pushed it above the 20-day EMA ($228). This up-move suggests that the immediate threat of a breakdown below the $200 support has decreased.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d94fe0204baede6b126caac8a003e92d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to propel the price above the downtrend line and the overhead resistance at $242. Above this level, the 50-day SMA ($254) could act as a resistance but when it is crossed, the rally may extend to $280.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day SMA is flattening out and the RSI has risen to the 50 level, which suggests a possible change in the short-term trend. If the price turns down from $242, the BCH/USD pair could consolidate for a few days before starting a trending move.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($25.52) on Sep.26 and has continued to move up. The next target objective is the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $27.7542.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e9fcd969f74fdede6aba14dcdbadc6e2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to stall the up-move at this level but if the next dip rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the correction could be over.\par \par \uc2 Above $27.7542, the up-move may extend to the 61.80% Fibonacci retracement level of $29.0886 and then to the 78.6% retracement level of $30.9884.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the BNB/USD pair reverses direction from the current levels and breaks below the moving averages, a retest of $22.10 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned around from $4.1152 on Sep. 27 and the bulls are now trying to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($4.60). A break above this resistance will suggest that the correction might be over.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2c4a0b5b93a03ac71c57ba82a9a863f7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $4.9210 and above this, the DOT/USD pair could move up to $5.5899. If the pair turns down from either level, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price above $5.5899, a retest of the recent highs at $6.8619 could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down and breaks below the $4\u8211\'20\'13$3.5321 support zone.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are defending the 20-day EMA ($10.76) but the bulls are not allowing Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) to sustain below $10. This suggests that the bulls are accumulating around the current levels and this tight consolidation increases the possibility of a break above the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e4ec69da1ed8ef4c23ab17b2d61c1c49.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $11.199, the downtrend could possibly be over. The next target on the upside is $13.28 and if the bulls can push the price above this resistance, the up-move can reach $17.77.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears defend the $13.28 resistance, the LINK/USD pair may turn down and remain range-bound for a few days. The flat moving averages and the RSI near the 50 level also indicates a possible consolidation.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the $6.90 support.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The relief rally in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) surged above the 20-day EMA ($0.094) on Sep. 25 and the bulls are now attempting to push the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.109). If they succeed, it will suggest that the downtrend has ended.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/98a429e8fda7d75e7133b6bbaa0824ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is gradually turning up and the RSI has also risen into the positive territory, which shows that the bulls are making a comeback. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair breaks out and closes (UTC time) above the 50-day SMA, the up-move can reach $0.1280.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the current levels, the bulls will try to buy the dip to the 20-day EMA. A strong bounce off this support will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive.\par \par \uc2 This view will be negated if the pair turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA. Such a move could retest the recent lows at $0.0755701.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($165) on Sep. 26 and the bulls are now trying to push the price above the 50-day SMA ($182). However, the bears are likely to pose a stiff challenge at this resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d6aaa0c3ea364e266a97963b8ef4bddc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 50-day SMA and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the bears will again try to sink the BSV/USD pair below the $146.20\u8211\'20\'13$135.00 support zone.\par \par \uc2 However, the RSI has risen into the positive territory and the 20-day EMA is trying to turn up, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can propel the price above the 50-day SMA, the pair can move up to $208.10 and then to $227.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to drive Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.157) and the resistance line of the descending triangle. If they succeed, it will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b8e896d2ec9680be42d703787dbbce60.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup traps several aggressive bears who have gone short anticipating the prices to fall. They are then forced to cover their positions at higher levels, fueling a rally.\par \par \uc2 In this case, if the price closes (UTC time) above the triangle, the CRO/USD pair could move up to $0.183416 and above it to $0.191101.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from either the 20-day EMA or the resistance line, the bears will once again try to sink the price below $0.144743. If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal pattern will complete and may result in a deeper correction.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy8zMmY0MjVhNTZmN2FmYWU4NzRlZGJiNzIyMDNjYzVmNy5qcGVn.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200928eg9s000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Top 5 cryptocurrencies to watch this week: BTC, NEO, XMR,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LINK\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,701 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is attempting to form a bottom altcoins continue to decline, which opens up opportunities on the long and the short side\par \par \uc2 The total crypto market capitalization has recovered from the Sep. 6 lows near $314 billion but it is struggling to sustain above the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/charts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $350 billion}}}\uc2  mark, which shows that higher levels continue to attract sellers.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) dominance fell from above 68% in mid-May to about 56% in the first half of this month as DeFi tokens embarked on a strong bull run.\par \par \uc2 However, in the past few days, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-celebrities-charged-and-kiss-bad-crypto-news-of-the-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeFi assets have witnessed sharp corrections}}}\uc2  and their \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased. This could possibly shift traders\u8217\'20\'19 attention back to Bitcoin. It\u8217\'20\'19s also possible that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s inability to hold above the $11,000 level could also be negatively weighing on the confidence of altcoin and DeFi-token traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/caf643cac70482bbb2e5a292d32ed395.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto market data daily view}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-fpje2fq19a_1589129732773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Although Bitcoin has been struggling to find momentum, a positive is that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-bitcoin-bull-run-whales-and-institutions-accumulating-data-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 volume of Bitcoin futures trading on Bakkt has been increasing}}}\uc2  and the exchange whale ratio is near yearly lows. This suggests accumulation by the whales and institutional traders.\par \par \uc2 Currently, most major cryptocurrencies are not following a general trend as the price action has been mostly coin specific. This has opened up opportunities both on the short side and the long side. Hence, in today\u8217\'20\'19s list, two short ideas have been discussed for the traders who are \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the crypto markets.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The relief rally in Bitcoin is facing stiff resistance near the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $11,147.60. This shows that the bears have used the current relief rally to initiate short positions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e0649f7360df3fa6d7e52cc16501a47d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the price below the uptrend line and the $10,625 support, it will signal weakness. If the BTC/USD pair sustains below $10,625, it will increase the possibility of a retest of $9,835.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off the $10,625 support sharply, this will be the first sign that the correction might be over. Trading momentum is likely to pick up after the rally breaks above the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 If the price closes (UTC time) above the downtrend line, the possibility of a rally to $12,460 increases. Even though there is resistance at $12,000 it seems likely that it will be crossed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a966f3bfbfa44668ba0ededadc03c4c7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The pair is currently attempting to rebound off the uptrend line, which suggests that the bulls purchased the dip to this support. The buyers will now make one more attempt to push the price above the $11,147.60 resistance.\par \par \uc2 If the bounce fizzles out and the bears sink the pair below the uptrend line, a drop to $10,625 could occur. This is an important support for the bulls because selling is likely to intensify if this level breaks down.\par \par \uc2 If the pair rebounds off $10,625, a few days of range-bound action is possible. The flattening moving average on the 4-hour chart suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 NEO/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/neo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEO}}}\uc2  is currently facing stiff resistance at $25.23, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this resistance. However, as it is in an uptrend, traders are likely to view the dips as a buying opportunity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d7614d1eddd39ec9335ef0faed1f266c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEO/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 NEO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/NEOUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The immediate support on the downside is at $23 and below that at the 10-day simple moving average ($22.26). If the NEO/USD pair rebounds off either support, it will indicate that the bulls are not waiting for a deeper fall to buy which is a positive sign.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the $25.23\u8211\'20\'13$25.78923 resistance zone, the uptrend is likely to resume. The next target on the upside is $29.\par \par \uc2 A break below the 10-day SMA will be the first sign that the momentum is weakening and a drop below $20.9633 will signal a possible change in trend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/dd51dffbf268b983a20314156b34ff40.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEO/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 NEO/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/NEOUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bulls pushed the price above the $25.23 resistance twice but they could not sustain the higher levels. This shows that the bears are attempting to stall the rally at this resistance.\par \par \uc2 However, on the downside, the bulls have not allowed the price to sustain below $23, which shows that the buyers are accumulating on every minor dip.\par \par \uc2 This could keep the pair stuck between $23 and $25.50 for a few more days. The moving averages have flattened out, which suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD\par \par \uc2 The recovery in Monero ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xmr-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR}}}\uc2  ) from the Sep. 5 low of $74.1012 has been strong and the bulls have pushed the price back above the moving averages, which increases the possibility that the correction might be over.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/fd2b41dcfaedf3afb51967eae8a2386f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up without a stiff fight at the $97.4615 resistance. If the XMR/USD pair turns down sharply from the current levels and breaks below $84, a drop to $74.1012 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can arrest the next dip at the 20-day exponential moving average ($89), it will increase the possibility of a breakout of $97.4615. Above this resistance, a move to $105.9131\u8211\'20\'13$107.3742 is possible. A break above $107.3742 can result in a rally to $120.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7949fc93ee1582473fd6ef82e98ed7c5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XMR/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XMRUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the recovery from $74.1012 has been gradual. Although the bears broke the pair below the 30-EMA on several occasions, they could not capitalize on it and intensify the selling.\par \par \uc2 This shows that the bulls are accumulating on dips. Currently, the price has again dipped back below the 30-EMA. If the pair rebounds off the current levels, the bulls will try and drive the price above the overhead resistance at $97.4615.\par \par \uc2 The short-term momentum is likely to weaken if the bears can break and sustain the price below the immediate support at $87.5629.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The relief rally in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) from the lows of $0.0855982 on Sep. 6 hit a stiff resistance at $0.0997444 on Sep. 13. The moving averages are sloping down, which suggests that the bears are in command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/c47999762ecdcf29dadd617b2d03e526.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 In a downtrend, the bears short on pullbacks to resistance levels as that improves the risk to reward ratio of the trade. Currently, if the bears can sink the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair below the $0.0855982 support, the decline might resume.\par \par \uc2 Traders can consider taking positions on the short side with an appropriate stop-loss to benefit from the likely down move. The next support on the downside is at $0.074 but if this support fails to hold, the drop can extend to $0.05.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair rebounds off $0.0855982 and the bulls drive the price above $0.10. Such a move will suggest that the downtrend might be over.\par \par \uc2 However, it is not necessary that a new uptrend starts as soon as a downtrend ends because many times, the price remains range-bound as it tries to form a bottom.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, traders can step aside and wait for a new \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup to form if the price breaks above $0.10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4dca266a6ead56a0d4499ba0aa3162d6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the pair has been gradually declining towards the critical support at $0.0855982 and a close (UTC time) below this level is likely to start the next leg of the down move.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off $0.0855982, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the price above $0.10. If they succeed, a quick relief rally is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price again turns down from $0.10, the pair might remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) is in a downtrend and it has been making a lower high and a lower low pattern for the past few days, which shows that the bears are using the relief rallies to sell.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2bf1de22a5b6416a46d2acdecc958849.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The down sloping moving averages suggest that the trend favors the bears. If they can sink the LINK/USD pair below $9.65, a drop to $9 is likely. This is an important support to watch out for because a break below this level is likely to resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 The next support on the downside is $7. Therefore, traders can consider benefiting from the possible down-move.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns up from the current levels or rebounds off sharply from the $9 levels and breaks above the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b10c16d606d46b2d191bebf4ffdc51bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD 4-hour chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 On Sep. 5 and 6, the bears were unable to sustain the price below $10.50, which shows that the bulls were attempting to defend this level.\par \par \uc2 However, during the current fall, the price has been sustaining below $10.50 for the past two days, which suggests that the buying has dried up.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are sloping down gradually and the price is below the averages, which suggests that the advantage is with the bears.\par \par \uc2 A break above the 30-EMA will be the first sign that the bears are losing their grip. Until then, the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9kZDY2YTNmYTFkYzA4ZTE3YjUzNzMyYTFkMzYwZTM4My5qcGVn.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200920eg9k000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 DeFi boom leaves former altcoin darlings in the dust \u8212\'20\'14 But for how long?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Madeira \par \uc2 850 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The strong performance from DeFi tokens has far eclipsed that of many top-10 altcoins but how long can this trend last?\par \par \uc2 The rapid popularity and investment growth observed in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Decentralized Finance}}}\uc2  (DeFi) sector has reflected heavily on the price charts with DeFi and yield-related tokens like Yearn.finance ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/yearn-finance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YFI}}}\uc2  ), Aave ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/aave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEND}}}\uc2  ), and others rallying to their all-time highs in 2020. YFI alone has surged 10x since listing.\par \par \uc2 In fact, most high-profile DeFi-related tokens have outperformed Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and other altcoins by a long stretch. Even governance and infrastructure projects like Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/chainlink/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) and UMA, the latter of which became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uma-overtakes-yearnfinance-as-the-biggest-defi-protocol-on-ethereum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the largest DeFi protocols}}}\uc2  in September, were eclipsed by DeFi tokens.\par \par \uc2 As so, with all eyes set on DeFi projects and smart contract platforms like Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), a few sectors in the cryptocurrency world appear to have been left behind. Most noticeably, coss-payment platforms like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  and Stellar ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9f0ee02f2e08f4fdbb75849752af75d6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Comparison of profits and losses since December 2018}}}\par \par \uc2 Comparison of profits and losses since December 2018. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nsquaredcrypto/status/1299332770842501120?s=21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CaneIsland Digital Research}}}\par \par \uc2 Although smart contract platforms like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/eos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EOS}}}\uc2  have made modest gains, it has failed to keep up with competitors like Ether, which has been the epicenter of the 2020 DeFi craze (as most DeFi-related tokens are Ethereum ERC20 tokens).\par \par \uc2 Ripple loses its allure\par \par \uc2 Among the top-10 coins by market cap XRP has been one of the worst performers in 2020, having recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/tether-surpasses-xrp-by-market-cap-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost its position as the third biggest altcoin}}}\uc2  to Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/tether/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ). Ripple is currently the fourth biggest cryptocurrency with a market capitalization of roughly $10.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 While XRP has risen 20% since the start of 2020 it lags far behind Bitcoin and many other altcoins. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://research.binance.com/en/analysis/is-the-crypto-market-turning-into-a-kangaroo-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance\u8217\'20\'19s Q2 report}}}\uc2 , the exchange revealed that XRP is the fifth worst-performing crypto on the platform.\par \par \uc2 There have also been multiple public issues with the project such as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/lawsuit-investors-cant-prove-ripple-knew-xrp-had-no-utility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-lasting class-action lawsuit}}}\uc2  regarding the marketing and sale of the XRP token. Ripple is also facing a copyright-related lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ripple-faces-lawsuit-in-australia-over-payid-branding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over the use of the \u8220\'20\'1CPayID\u8221\'20\'1D brand}}}\uc2 . Most recently, Santander, one of Ripple\u8217\'20\'19s key bank partners, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-santander-doesnt-want-to-use-ripple-for-international-payments-yet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed concerns}}}\uc2  when it comes to adopting One Pay FX, Ripple\u8217\'20\'19s international payment network.\par \par \uc2 While things look grim for XRP, there are a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ripple-ceo-fires-back-at-nyt-reporter-ripple-has-no-plans-to-reset-our-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 few positive signs for the project}}}\uc2 , such as the growth of On-Demand Liquidity which has processed over $2 billion in transactions since launch and has seen an 11x growth in the first half of 2020, when compared to the first half of 2019.\par \par \uc2 There are also plans to move closer to the DeFi space with XRP partner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/flare-proposes-new-bridge-to-allow-xrp-to-be-used-on-ethereum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Flare Networks announcing a project}}}\uc2  that aims to bridge the Ripple and Ethereum blockchains.\par \par \uc2 Privacy coins were also left behind\par \par \uc2 Cross-border payments do not seem to be a hot topic in crypto at the moment, given the speculation around DeFi and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/stablecoin-market-cap-increases-by-100m-every-single-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growth in stablecoin use}}}\uc2 . However, there are other pockets that have also failed to perform as well as DeFi or even as well as Bitcoin, including privacy coins.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://messari.io/screener/privacy-coins-vs-btc-924FDD3E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from Messari}}}\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  data company, Bitcoin has outperformed many of the privacy coins in the market, although popular coins like Monero ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/coin/monero-xmr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XMR}}}\uc2  ) and Zcash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/coin/zcash-zec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ZEC}}}\uc2  ) have seen modest gains in comparison to Bitcoin in the last 12 months, roughly 5% and 20% respectively.\par \par \uc2 The tables will turn when the DeFi bubble pops\par \par \uc2 While DeFi-related tokens have generated accentuated gains for holders in 2020, the craze has also generated a host of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/how-can-defi-projects-avoid-getting-cloned-and-dying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clone and meme projects}}}\uc2  that are capitalizing on the hype.\par \par \uc2 Some tokens in the DeFi sector have taken massive hits to their value, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-defends-sushi-listing-after-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including the SUSHI token}}}\uc2 , whose main developer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sushiswap-head-chef-dumps-tokens-plans-to-focus-on-migration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 market sold a significant number of tokens}}}\uc2  in what some people believe was an exit scam. Another DeFi meme-token which made media waves recently was Hotdog. The food-themed token {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-meme-coin-hotdog-dumps-99-9-in-hours-after-launch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost 99% of its value in the span of 5 minutes}}}\uc2 , leaving many investors holding worthless bags of hotdogs.\par \par \uc2 While DeFi has been leaving other sectors in the cryptosphere behind, users should be aware that many of these new projects have very little to offer, being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/five-years-since-launch-is-ethereum-creating-a-new-boom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reminiscent of the ICO space in 2017}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As so, the DeFi sector may soon follow the same footsteps, especially as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-gas-fees-reach-500k-as-eth-price-hits-a-2020-high-at-486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum blockchain continues to be overwhelmed}}}\uc2 . If this happens, it is likely that profits will go {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/alt-season-is-here-defi-tokens-taking-on-bitcoin-for-crypto-dominance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back to Bitcoin to fiat/stablecoins or to other sectors of crypto}}}\uc2  that have been left out of the current hype.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, DeFi has shown few signs of slowing down anytime soon, especially as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/yearnfinances-140m-yeth-vault-proves-investors-are-ravenous-for-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high-yield automated strategies continue to be developed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the future, it\u8217\'20\'19s possible that a portion of these profits will trickle back into Bitcoin and altcoins as investors look for \u8216\'20\'18safer\u8217\'20\'19 assets to earn interest in. Thus, it might not be necessary for non-DeFi coins and networks to develop new use cases to entice investors.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy82ZTFjMmRhZDAxMmZkMjM4YWRkZjQ2NzY4NWVmOGE3MC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200907eg97000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BNB, CRO, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,765 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  patterns on Bitcoin and altcoins complete the current correction could see prices drop to new lows\par \par \uc2 The U.S. stock market continues to hit new all-time highs while gold, which acts as a safe haven asset has retreated from it's all-time highs. This suggests that there sentiment is to own risky assets. Meanwhile, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), which at times behaves as an uncorrelated asset, remains stuck in a range.\par \par \uc2 However, with the U.S. presidential elections approaching, the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all the markets is likely to pick up.\par \par \uc2 If President Donald Trump is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/expect-market-regulation-avalanche-if-biden-beats-trump-mulvaney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 re-elected}}}\uc2 , then there is unlikely to be a huge change in the current economic policies. If Joe Biden wins the election, then economists, traders and corporations are likely to remain cautious for a few weeks and this could lead to a correction as markets hate uncertainty. Therefore, traders should get ready for a roller-coaster ride for the next few months.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b2e4b93db8ac614690ff2bb24f459bfa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-is-targeting-288k-stock-to-flow-price-like-clockwork-planb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to PlanB, the creator of the popular stock-to-flow model}}}\uc2 , Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price action after its halving in May has been closely following the model. If Bitcoin continues to follow the model, then the price is likely to skyrocket within a few months and embark on a long-term bull market, with a target objective of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-mirrors-gains-of-past-halvings-suggesting-41k-price-in-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $288,000}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the long-term picture might look \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , what do the charts project for the short-term?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study them to find out!\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has once again turned down from the $12,113.50 overhead resistance, which suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2da0a21e3663f57f6aa126bf3cd5ee90.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Currently, the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,558) has flattened out and the relative strength index is just below the midpoint, which suggests a balance between the bulls and the bears.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink and sustain the price below the $11,000 support, it will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern, which has a pattern target of $9,540.\par \par \uc2 It is unlikely to be a straight fall to the target because the bulls will attempt to defend the $10,400\u8211\'20\'13$10,000 zone aggressively.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the $11,000 levels, the BTC/USD pair is likely to remain range-bound for a few days. The trend will shift in favor of the bulls if they can scale the price above the $12,113.50\u8211\'20\'13$12,460 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 The next few days are critical because the breakout or breakdown from the $11,000\u8211\'20\'13$12,113.50 range could start the next directional move.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) surged above the overhead resistance of $446.479 on Sep. 1 and hit its first target objective of $480. This attracted a huge bout of profit booking from traders that resulted in a sharp intraday fall to $416.248 today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/5e6807b9b139a84ddd0ecf3e92b16999.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the 20-day EMA ($408), which is a positive sign as it shows that the positive sentiment remains intact.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is still in the positive zone, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand. However, they will have to push the price above the $480 resistance for the uptrend to resume.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the ETH/USD pair below $415.634, a drop to $366 is possible. A break below this support will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  rallied just above the $0.295813 level on Sep. 1 and the bulls tried to resume the up-move today but they encountered huge selling pressure at $0.303746 and this pulled the the price to $0.262484.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/3790c407ca2f2947ea48387b30d3df11.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The positive sign is that the bulls purchased the dip to the 50-day simple moving average ($0.263) again today, which makes this a critical level to watch out for. If the bears sink the price below this support, the possibility of a deeper fall to $0.235688 increases.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls defend the 50-day SMA, the XRP/USD pair could remain range-bound between $0.26\u8211\'20\'13$0.30 for a few days. On a close (UTC time) above $0.30, a move to $0.326113 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA ($0.280) and the RSI just below the 50 level suggests a balance between supply and demand, with a minor advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) attempted to bounce off the 20-day EMA ($14.99) on Sep. 01 but a sharp reversal today resulted in a decline to $14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a4e82a02173722b8de41952a2d48b3a8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has dipped close to the midpoint, which suggests that the LINK/USD pair could remain range-bound between $12.89 and $17.7777 for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $12.89, it will be a huge negative as that will form a lower high and a lower low pattern, which will suggest that the uptrend has ended.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls manage to push the pair above $17.7777, a retest of the highs at $20.1111 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($280) on Sep. 1 but that victory for the bulls was short-lived as the altcoin reversed sharply today, which suggests that bears are selling aggressively at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/95fe9c48a4641c5527a7eebeb15dfd06.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BCH/USD pair has bounced off $245.63 today, which is just above the intraday low of $245 made on Aug. 2. This is an important support to watch out for because if it cracks, a drop to $217.55 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI has again dropped into the negative territory, which suggests that bears have the upper hand. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair rises and sustains above the $280 resistance.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) stayed above the 20-day EMA ($59.31) for the past two days but the bulls could not push the price above the $64 resistance, which suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e21a971d8ff7d02edc112f46f839d10a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The LTC/USD pair has formed a possible head and shoulders pattern, which will complete on a breakdown and close (UTC time) below the neckline. This setup has a target objective of $39.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off the 50-day SMA ($55.36) or the neckline, the bulls will again attempt to push the price above $64. If they succeed, a rally to $68.90 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke out of the $24.4588 overhead resistance on Sep. 1, which suggested a resumption of the up-move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a7c7c5a901e9d5f4582850cec6bbab87.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the BNB/USD pair reversed direction sharply from $25.8262 today. The only positive thing is that the bears could not sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($22.85), which suggests strong buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that the advantage is with the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the pair rises above $24.4588 once again, it is likely to rally to $27.1905 and if this level is scaled, a move to $32 is possible. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair breaks below $20.5710.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the breakout level of $0.176596, which suggests profit booking at higher levels. If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.171), a drop to the 50-day SMA ($0.162) is likely.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e07cb6e99e6aae71e5436e786e45434f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the 20-day EMA is gradually sloping up and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the CRO/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will once again try to push the price above the $0.176596\u8211\'20\'13$0.183416 resistance zone. If they succeed, a retest of $0.191101 is likely.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $200 overhead resistance on Sep. 1 but that proved to be a bull trap as the price turned down sharply today and fell to an intraday low of $173.53.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2c9cf19c1ff3c7cc731ea29997ff2042.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The next support on the downside is $160 and if that also cracks, a retest of $146.20 will be on the cards. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($198) and the RSI in the negative zone suggest advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the BSV/USD pair turns around from the current levels and breaks out of the downtrend line. Such a move will suggest that bulls are back in the game.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the $0.10 critical support in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) hit a barrier just below the previous support turned resistance of $0.13, which suggests that the bears are selling on rallies to critical resistance levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/6e1e8344e1fa2a62822264c1a523dd7b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.122) is sloping down and the RSI is in the negative territory, which suggests that bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair below the $0.10 support, it will be a huge negative as it will suggest the possible start of a new downtrend. The next support on the downside is way lower at $0.08.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls defend the $0.10 support, the pair could remain range-bound for a few days. The trend will shift in favor of the bulls on a close (UTC time) above $0.13.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy84M2NkZWQxMzIzMGJkNWE0NjBiYjQ4NDE0ZmJjN2Q2Yy5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200902eg92000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 8/26: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BSV, CRO, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,745 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins are likely to remain range-bound in the short-term as the bulls and the bears attempt to assert their dominance\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, U.S. Federal Reserve chairman Jerome Powell is expected to deliver an important speech that will highlight a new strategy of targeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/08/24/powell-set-to-deliver-profoundly-consequential-speech-changing-how-the-fed-views-inflation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Caverage inflation.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  This means that the Fed might allow inflation to overshoot the 2% target temporarily if it has spent a long time below that level.\par \par \uc2 If the Fed adopts this new strategy, it could keep interest rates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/tyler-winklevoss-says-us-fed-is-the-biggest-booster-of-bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near zero}}}\uc2  for five years or more, according to a Bloomberg report.\par \par \uc2 The abundant liquidity is likely to drive asset prices higher across the board and create bubbles that will eventually burst. If this occurs, investors are likely to lose complete faith in the central banks and fiat currencies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9cc7713bf11455e53ff9c3e176fc3075.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Smart investors are likely to seek the safety of gold and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) during this time of uncertainty. Larger investors have already started {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/record-high-bitcoin-whale-population-is-bullish-for-btc-price-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accumulating Bitcoin}}}\uc2  and this has pushed the number of addresses holding over 1,000 BTC to a new record high.\par \par \uc2 While this is all great news, traders will want to know if the crypto market will extend it\u8217\'20\'19s current up-move or whether a period of extended consolidation is at hand.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out!\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin plunged and closed (UTC time) below the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,554) on Aug. 25, which is the first indication that the bulls were losing their grip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/41234c567dbb516249ef7a08b514923f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the $11,100\u8211\'20\'13$10,900 support zone but are likely to face significant resistance at the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price back above the 20-day EMA, a drop to the 50-day simple moving average ($10,728) and then to $10,400 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, a move to $12,113.50 is likely. The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index is just above the midpoint, which suggests a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \uc2 The next trending move is likely to start after the bulls push the price above the $12,113.50\u8211\'20\'13$12,460 resistance zone or sink the price below the $10,400\u8211\'20\'1310,000 support zone.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above the $415.634 resistance on Aug. 24 attracted profit booking on Aug. 25 that pulled down the price to the critical support at $366.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b04426e334216fb931297e6904c8d9c3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the bulls purchased the dip on Aug. 25, they are struggling to push the ETH/USD pair above the 20-day EMA ($393), which is a negative sign. This shows a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 A break and close (UTC time) below $366 could intensify selling and result in a drop to the 50-day SMA ($336). Such a move will suggest that a short-term top has been made at $446.479.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, a few days of range-bound action between $366\u8211\'20\'13 $415.634 is likely.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  closed (UTC time) above the 20-day EMA ($0.284) on Aug. 24 but a lack of buying at higher levels again pulled down the price to the $0.268478 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/25b8b0aae7921fa5ad48a502e5d1e29c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the $0.268478 support but unless they sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the advantage will remain with the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the XRP/USD pair below $0.268478, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($0.25) is possible. This is an important support to watch out for because if it cracks, the decline can extend to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.241068.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair rebounds off the $0.268478 support and rises above the 20-day EMA, then a few days of range-bound action between $0.326113 and $0.268478 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to push Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance of $16 on Aug. 23 and 24, which attracted profit booking that pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA ($14.49) on Aug. 25.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/270f1fbead2c95d0a6c08b4da99d20e4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the positive thing is that the lower levels are attracting buying by the bulls, which shows that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Currently, the LINK/USD pair has again risen above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can propel the price above $16, LINK will attempt to resume the uptrend and retest the highs at $20.1111.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the pair again turns down from $16, the bears will try to sink the price to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $11.9281.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound from the breakout level of $280 in Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($288) on Aug. 25, which suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1d2813e7ee5a08557e42bf368e7ba9cc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip to the 50-day SMA ($271) on Aug. 25 but if they fail to push the price back above $280, it is likely to attract another round of selling that could sink the BCH/USD pair to $260 and then to $240.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that bears have made a comeback.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair rebounds off the current levels and rises above the $280\u8211\'20\'13$295 resistance.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned around and plunged below the 20-day EMA ($59) on Aug. 25, which suggests selling by the bears on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9822c9a7b4ca456a449431336820b091.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The next support on the downside is the 50-day SMA ($53) and if this support also gives way, a drop to $51 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the LTC/USD pair rebounds off the current levels, the bulls will attempt to push the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, a move to $64 and then to $68.9008 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance of $200 but could not clear the 20-day EMA ($206) hurdle on Aug. 24, which attracted selling on Aug. 25 that pulled the altcoin back below $200.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2c7589acc4863caf33f85239f0b4c1ec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative zone, which suggests that the bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price back above $200 within the next few days, the BSV/USD pair is likely to slide to $160 and then to $146.20.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls can push the price back above the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance of $0.176596 on Aug. 25, which suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ca1deb00429159e3f40501a785c9c34b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, both moving averages are gradually sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that the bulls are at a minor advantage.\par \par \uc2 If the CRO/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($0.166), the bulls will once again attempt to scale the price above $0.176596. If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to resume. The first target on the upside is $0.191101 and then $0.20.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($0.157) is possible.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance of $22.93 on Aug. 25 and dropped below the 20-day EMA ($22), which suggests aggressive selling by the bears at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/f93d426dc6f92b0b9eaf31d0aa49b956.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears could not capitalize on the opportunity and sink the BNB/USD pair below the critical support at $20.5710.\par \par \uc2 This has attracted buying from the aggressive bulls who are attempting to push the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, a move to $22.93 and then to $23.91 is likely.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the pair turns down from the downtrend line and plummets below $20.5710, a deeper correction to $19.10 is possible.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) plunged to the $0.10\u8211\'20\'13$0.11 support zone on Aug. 25, which is a negative sign. The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative territory, suggesting advantage to the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/386939a42978515f4f19d3e58aa335c5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Currently, the bulls are attempting to defend the support zone aggressively. However, any recovery is likely to face stiff resistance from the 20-day EMA ($0.129). If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears will attempt to sink the price below $0.10.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will be a huge negative as the next support on the downside is way lower at $0.075.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the bulls can push the price back above the 20-day EMA and the overhead resistance at $0.13.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy82MGMzNmE0NzA4MDZiYTVlNTg1NTViOGU5MWRkYTE5Ni5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200826eg8q000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 8/24: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC, BSV, CRO, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bulls are aggressively defending the 20-day EMA in Bitcoin and select altcoins, which could result in the resumption of the uptrend\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus pandemic has forced people to change several social behavioral habits. Along with maintaining social distance from one another, people are also averse to using notes, coins or cards as they might transmit COVID-19.\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/public-interest-in-central-bank-digital-currencies-surpasses-bitcoin-in-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank for International Settlements\uc2  suggested that social distancing procedures and the \u8220\'20\'1Cgovernment-to-person payment schemes\u8221\'20\'1D have accelerated the efforts towards launching central bank digital currencies (CBDCs). The paper shows that the public interest in CBDCs has exceeded that of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Libra in 2020.\par \par \uc2 However, the CBDCs will only be a digital version of the fiat currencies that will be controlled by the central banks. Hence, the problems that plague the U.S. dollar currently will even affect the digital version of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, after people familiarize with CBDCs and realize their ease of use, they are likely to warm up to cryptocurrencies due to their inherent advantages over fiat currencies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1502c1b9ff8bb6a59a094095adb3417f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Even with its numerous advantages, Bitcoin continues to have its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/i-would-never-invest-one-cent-in-bitcoin-says-ryanair-ceo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 naysayers}}}\uc2 . Ryanair CEO Micheal O\u8217\'20\'19Leary painted a very \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  picture of Bitcoin and said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cequivalent to a Ponzi scheme\u8221\'20\'1D. This shows how several institutional investors are still wary of cryptocurrencies but retail traders have been quick to embrace the new asset class.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are defending the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,589), which is a positive sign as it indicates that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bitcoin could now move up to the $12,113.50 resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a95875970a2855088804ec03598029e5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is gradually sloping up and the relative strength index is in the positive zone, which suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can propel the price above the $12,113.50\u8211\'20\'13$12,460 resistance zone, the uptrend is likely to resume with the next target at $13,000 and then $14,000.\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are unlikely to give up without a fight. They will again mount a stiff resistance at $12,113.50. If the BTC/USD pair turns down from this zone, a drop to $11,000 and then to $10,400 is possible.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) repeatedly slipped below the 20-day EMA ($394) for three consecutive days between Aug. 21 to 23 but the bears could not intensify the selling and pull the price down to $366, which suggests that the bulls were accumulating at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/29e7d03899d53986e90797adeadc859f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Currently, the bulls are attempting to push the ETH/USD pair above the $415.634 resistance. If they succeed, a retest of $446.479 is likely. A breakout of this level will signal the possible resumption of the uptrend, with the next target objective at $480 and then $516.11.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from either $415.634 or $446.479, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint also suggests a consolidation for a few days. The trend will turn negative if the bears sink the price below the critical support at $366.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  is currently range-bound between $0.326113 and $0.268478. The 20-day EMA ($0.285) has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a balance between demand and supply.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9128fcadfbfa1b9e8792d0f21b7d53e6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This balance will shift in favor of the bulls if they can push the price above $0.326113. Above this level, a rally to $0.346727 and then to $0.40 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from $0.326113, it will extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will shift in favor of the bears if the XRP/USD pair breaks below the $0.268478 support. If this level cracks, a drop to $0.24 is likely.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have managed to defend the breakout level of $280, which suggests buying on dips. They will now try to push Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) to the overhead resistance at $326.30. The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/24b5865519de07e3740aa4668e5b5795.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $326.30, the BCH/USD pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price above $326.30, a rally to $353 is possible. A breakout of this resistance could result in a rally to $400.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the pair breaks and sustains below the $280 support. The next target on the downside is $260 and then $245.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $13.4906 on Aug. 21 but the price rebounded sharply on Aug. 22, which shows strong buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a40000c7af51e116851c380c5705a280.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The LINK/USD pair is currently trading above the 20-day EMA ($14.43), which is gradually sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, suggesting a slight advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $16, the pair is likely to pick up momentum and move up to $17.6738. A breakout of this level can result in a retest of $20.1111.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from $16, the bears will again try to sink the price below the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, a drop to $12.89 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($59.54) on Aug. 22 and 23 but the bears could not sustain the lower levels, which suggests accumulation by the bulls on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0fb8d3dc12a42d2af08305e5957749d7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Currently, the LTC/USD pair has bounced off the 20-day EMA and the bulls will try to push the price above the $65.1573\u8211\'20\'13$68.9008 resistance zone. If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to resume, with the next target at $80.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is also in the positive zone, which suggests that bulls are at an advantage.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the overhead resistance and breaks below the $57.7736 support.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke down of the $200 support on Aug. 21, which completed the descending triangle pattern. This setup has a pattern target objective of $142.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/edd98a7bce474568b6c51be4ffdcc204.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($209) is sloping down and the RSI is in the negative zone, which suggests that the bears have the upper hand. If the bears defend the breakdown level of $200, the BSV/USD pair is likely to drop to $160.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price back above $200 and the 20-day EMA, a move to the downtrend line of the triangle is possible. A break above this resistance will shift the advantage in favor of the bulls.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the 20-day EMA ($0.165) and the bulls will now try to push the price above the $0.176596 resistance. If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e89dd71035982aeb8ff804c7e7bc7df2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $0.191101 and if this level is scaled, the next target is $0.20. The 20-day EMA is gradually sloping up and the RSI is in the positive zone, which suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the CRO/USD pair turns down from the overhead resistance and breaks below the 20-day EMA. Such a move will suggest that the momentum has weakened. A break below $0.154322 could start a deeper correction.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($22.16) for three consecutive days between Aug. 21 to 23, but the bears could not sustain the price below the $21.7628 support, which suggests that the bulls are defending this support aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/676343d14dc660977419baa25d27bcb8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting a relief rally. If they can push the price above $22.93, a move to $24.4588 is possible. If this level is also scaled, the up move can extend to $27.1905.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the BNB/USD pair turns down from $22.93, the bears will once again attempt to sink and sustain the price below $21.7628. If they succeed, a drop to the 50-day simple moving average ($20.26) is likely.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) decisively broke below the $0.13 support on Aug. 21, which points to a possible change in trend. The 20-day EMA ($0.132) has started to slope down and the RSI is in the negative territory, suggesting advantage to the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1222e327a6f80a77cbb6eec22a56b61d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The first target objective on the downside is $0.11 and if that breaks, a drop to $0.10 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are unlikely to give up without a fight. They will try to push the price back above $0.13 and the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will suggest strong demand at lower levels but if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the downtrend is likely to resume.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9lZWRmOTI5ODI1NjRiMjZlODJkMDc4YWZiMGY4ZmU2MC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200824eg8o000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/21: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,848 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and several altcoins have formed \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergences, which suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened\par \par \uc2 Rich Dad Poor Dad author Robert Kiyosaki believes that Warren Buffet\u8217\'20\'19s recent closure of his bank stock positions is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/buy-bitcoin-before-major-banking-crisis-rich-dad-poor-dad-author"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning sign}}}\uc2  that the world might be starting a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor banking crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D Therefore, Kiyosaki suggests traders buy safe haven assets such as gold, silver and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) to protect themselves from the downward spiraling value of the fiat currencies.\par \par \uc2 Popular Bitcoin derivatives trader Tone Vays believes that Bitcoin could breakout to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/50k-bitcoin-is-reasonable-if-btc-hits-new-highs-says-tone-vays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new all-time highs}}}\uc2  in 2021. He pointed out that historically, Bitcoin has tended to double in price after breaking out of its all-time high, especially if it took years to do that. Hence, if Bitcoin breaks above $20,000, Vays expects a rally to at least \u8220\'20\'1C$45,000 to $50,000.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7e1fc2a038e4dbaef2f333d445194ebb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-bitcoin-market-looks-like-2016-before-historic-bull-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by Grayscale Investments suggests that the current market conditions are similar to the one seen in 2016 before Bitcoin began its stellar bull run. Grayscale highlights the growing dependence of the U.S. economy on expansionary monetary policy and believes that it will be very difficult to reverse it. This could stoke inflation, which will be \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 While these are long-term projections, in the short-term, the total crypto market capitalization has slid from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/charts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $380 billion}}}\uc2  on Aug. 17 to about $360 billion, which shows profit booking by short-term traders.\par \par \uc2 Investors will now want to know if the current correction will deepen or if the prices rebound in the coming days. Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out!\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Given that Bitcoin has been in a strong uptrend, traders have consistently purchased dips to the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,570) because they believe that the rally will resume and the price would not dip to these levels again.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/61267839d5c87489360b57da5794ee50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s weak rebound off the 20-day EMA on Aug. 20 suggests that the bulls are not confident that the uptrend will resume, hence, they are not buying aggressively at this support.\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the relative strength index suggests that the momentum has weakened. If the price breaks and sustains below the 20-day EMA, the traders are likely to wait for the BTC/USD pair to find support at lower levels, before buying.\par \par \uc2 On a drop below the 20-day EMA, the decline can extend to the $11,100\u8211\'20\'1310,900 support zone.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make another attempt to push the price above the $12,113.50\u8211\'20\'13$12,460 resistance zone. If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to resume.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the 20-day EMA ($395) on Aug. 20 fizzled out close to $415.634, which suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this resistance. They will now try to sink Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/72162c3b970ab5b34c6a0d862bbba392.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, a drop to $366 is possible. The bulls are likely to defend this support aggressively. A bounce off this support could keep the ETH/USD pair range-bound between $366\u8211\'20\'13$415.634 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the RSI shows that the momentum has weakened. If bears sink the pair below $366, a drop to the 50-day simple moving average ($321) is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the price above $415.634\u8211\'20\'13$446.479 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The weak rebound off the 20-day EMA ($0.285) on Aug. 20 suggests a lack of buyers at higher levels. If the bears can now sink {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $0.268478 is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/10282eb1794e39c7388cea418b757e3e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has dropped close to the midpoint, which suggests a range-bound action in the short-term. A strong bounce off the $0.268478 support will signal strength and the bulls will try to push the price back to $0.326113.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the XRP/USD pair below $0.268478, a deeper correction to the 50-day SMA ($0.243) is likely.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to stay above the 20-day EMA ($293), which suggests a lack of buying interest among the bulls. The altcoin can now drop to the $280 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0af5a37a3bf087032ecc3e041247175a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the 50 level suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink and sustain the BCH/USD pair below $280, it will be a huge negative as it would suggest a lack of buyers at higher levels. The next support on the downside is at the 50-day SMA ($266).\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off $280, the bulls will once again attempt to carry the price to $326.30.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) formed consecutive inside day candlestick patterns on Aug. 19 and 20, which showed indecision among traders. This was resolved to the downside today when the altcoin broke below the $14.69 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/3f168d80c7ed14cbf74718c536f78118.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the 20-day EMA ($14.12). If they succeed, the LINK/USD pair could rise to $17.6738. The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a range-bound action in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink and sustain the pair below the 20-day EMA, a drop to the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $13.4906 and below it to the 61.8% retracement level of $11.9281 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls defended the 20-day EMA ($59) on Aug. 19 but they could not push \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) to the overhead resistance at $65.1573, which suggests a lack of demand at higher levels. This usually happens when traders believe they will get a better entry opportunity at lower levels if they wait for some time.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/5ac40d376799abd6fbc48b08562521d2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, a decline to $56 and below it to $51 is possible. Such a move will suggest that the momentum has weakened and could result in a range-bound action for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The gradually rising 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that