).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0b6907e7bd8bcdb7f3bbb5b90d9ee88d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the sentiment has changed from buy on dips to sell on rallies. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair closes (UTC time) below $0.125, a drop to the next support at $0.11 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has dipped into the negative territory, which suggests that the bears are making a comeback.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns up from the current levels and rises above the 20-day EMA. Such a move will indicate strong buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to stay above the 20-day EMA ($22.15), which suggests that the bulls are not buying aggressively at this support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4aa725955562741747ed780b09208104.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the $21.7628 support, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($19.86) is possible. Such a move will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a range-bound action in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the BNB/USD pair rises from the current levels and breaks above $24.4588, a rally to $27.1905 is possible.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between the 20-day EMA ($0.1638) and the overhead resistance of $0.176596 for the past few days. This shows that the bulls are defending the 20-day EMA, which is a positive sign.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/595f544b4d74ac71e5dfa837ee994c5c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Today, the bulls had pushed the price above $0.176596 but they could not sustain the higher levels, which shows selling by the bears on sharp rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the CRO/USD pair sustains above the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make another attempt to push the price above $0.176596. If the price closes (UTC time) above this level, a rally to $0.20 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears sink the pair below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $0.154322 is possible. A rebound off this support could keep the pair range-bound between $0.154322\u8211\'20\'13$0.176596 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9jYTU4Yjc0NjRjNjVlMTlkODdhZWU0ZjhlNmRlODJkOS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200821eg8l000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Regulation\par \b \uc2 The Challenge of Taxing Proof-of-Stake\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Kollen Post \par \uc2 1,130 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph examines the basis of Congress calling out the IRS for threatening to tax proof-of-stake rewards beyond their actual value\par \par \uc2 While being a relatively young correction to energy-intensive proof-of-work (PoW) network validation, proof-of-stake has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-history-and-evolution-of-proof-of-stake#:~:text=Proof%20of%20Stake%20(PoS)%20was,to%20maintain%20the%20Bitcoin%20network."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 existed in theory since 2012}}}\uc2 . However, rising market cap of PoS tokens like Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and Tezos (XTZ) over the past two years and Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s much-hyped but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/ethereum-20-staking-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 much-delayed shift}}}\uc2  from PoW to PoS have brought the subject to the forefront.\par \par \uc2 Alongside an overall increase in regulatory attention on crypto generally, PoS protocols are an area of much debate. One question highlighted by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/congresspeople-call-on-irs-to-take-it-easy-on-taxing-staking-rewards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent letter from several Congresspeople to the IRS}}}\uc2  is taxes. Specifically, the letter voiced worries about overtaxing staking rewards.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the IRS is really treading in new territory, so it\u8217\'20\'19s not a surprise that they have yet to put together comprehensive guidance on staking rewards. Congressman David Schweikert (R-AZ), whose office sent the letter to the IRS, told Cointelegraph that the main task was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust trying to get it on their radar.\u8221\'20\'1D He continued:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know they have some very smart people over there working on those issues. We\u8217\'20\'19re letting them know that there are those in Congress interested.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/from-taxes-to-transparency-the-irs-gets-schooled-on-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted in the past}}}\uc2 , educating the IRS is complicated. Staking is no exception.\par \par \uc2 Staking rewards and the question of earnings\par \par \uc2 Explained briefly, PoS replaces PoW\u8217\'20\'19s dependence on hardware with commitment to the network. A Bitcoin miner in 2020 needs to buy fleets of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/switching-bitcoin-to-100-asic-mining-could-increase-security-2000x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ASIC machines}}}\uc2  and scour the globe for cheap electricity sources to have a real chance at turning a profit in the cryptographic arms race. PoS puts forward a more utopian vision of contributors validating the network by demonstrating their continued investment in it.\par \par \uc2 Obviously, the PoW v. PoS debate is more complicated than that. Issues like 51% attacks or domination of PoS networks by the earliest pioneers come up. Nonetheless, as a means of running a network it\u8217\'20\'19s a vital and evolving technology. When it comes to taxes, however, it\u8217\'20\'19s mostly unmapped territory.\par \par \uc2 The argument that the recent letter to the IRS depends on is this: If you stake tokens most networks reward you with tokens. Tax authorities like the IRS might be tempted to regard these rewards as income, as if those rewards were returns on a stock investment. That, however, assumes a lot about the stability of token prices on a PoS network, especially given that staking itself limits liquidity, so the staker is not able to respond to short-term price movements.\par \par \uc2 PoSA and defense of staking in the face of dilution\par \par \uc2 The Proof of Stake Alliance (POSA) is an advocacy group that focuses on issues most pressing to PoS networks. The POSA also helped with the letter to the IRS. Evan Weiss is the founder of POSA, in addition to being Bison Trails\u8217\'20\'19 head of business operations. Speaking to Cointelegraph, Weiss commented on the distinction between mining and staking:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith mining, token ownership and security of the network are divorced, but in proof-of-stake networks token holders have to help secure these networks. And so these rewards affect nearly every token holder now. It is such a tax headache.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Providing the intellectual framework to the POSA\u8217\'20\'19s work is Abraham Sutherland, an adjunct law professor at the University of Virginia. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.taxnotes.com/tax-notes-today-federal/cryptocurrency/dilution-and-true-economic-gain-cryptocurrency-block-rewards/2020/08/17/2ctmc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paper published}}}\uc2  this week in Tax Notes, Sutherland and co-author Mattia Landoni of the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Boston\uc2  wrote of the dangers of dilution. They argue that staking increases tokens but not the network\u8217\'20\'19s overall value:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCryptocurrencies consist of several tokens (units of accounting) in a network. If one accepts the uncontroversial premise that the value of a cryptocurrency network does not depend on the exact number of tokens it contains, then the creation of new cryptocurrency units results in dilution. Unlike random fluctuations in network value, which can give rise to both capital gains and losses, this dilution is sure to happen and sure to be detrimental to the taxpayer\u8217\'20\'19s wealth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking with Cointelegraph, Sutherland explained the misconception of profiting from staking further:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe simple model is what if everybody stakes their tokens? Then you basically have the same thing as a pro-rata stock dividend or even just a stock split, which, of course, is not taxed because there's no gain there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Refining and expanding definitions\par \par \uc2 Sutherland took issue with the IRS\u8217\'20\'19s implication of protocols that back tokens in the profit or lack thereof of stakeholders:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere's kind of an assumption supported by the way the IRS looked at this in 2014 that these protocols are entities capable of making payments to people, but they're not. For tax purposes, they're not corporations and they're not doing anything as an actor in the traditional sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The question of protocols as legal entities relates to the ongoing debate over which tokens {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-death-of-the-ico-has-the-us-sec-closed-the-global-window-on-new-tokens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 qualify as securities}}}\uc2  i.e. investments in a company. Without clear policy from the IRS, taxpayers concerned about stringent crackdowns are left treating returns from decentralized protocols like those from the stock market.\par \par \uc2 Rather than the stock market, some people say the best analogy for staking is produce. If you have an apple tree on your property, the IRS can\u8217\'20\'19t tax you for apples growing on it, nor can they demand a slice out of every apple pie you make for personal consumption. They can, however, tax you if you bring your apples to market to sell. That seems to be POSA\u8217\'20\'19s point as well: The moment of sale for another currency is a clear and convenient taxable event for tokens earned through staking.\par \par \uc2 Chandan Lodha, a co-founder of crypto tax software Cointracker, told Cointelegraph that existing guidance just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t include the range of active cryptocurrencies, meaning that regulators are stuck trying to apply creaky analogies, like those of apples or stocks. He said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the industry matures, we need more specific guidance on how different emerging areas of cryptocurrency are taxed (e.g. staking) and legislation more explicitly defining how these taxes should work on cryptocurrencies \u8212\'20\'14 either by creating a new definition of what cryptocurrencies are, or by having more specific rules based on the type / use case of the cryptocurrency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shehan Chandrasekera, Cointracker\u8217\'20\'19s head of tax strategy, advised caution in the meantime: \u8220\'20\'1CIn the absence of IRS guidance, what taxpayers can do is take the most conservative approach, which is recognizing income at the time you receive it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that the IRS is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/irs-tax-warnings-on-ethereums-fifth-anniversary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paying ever-closer attention}}}\uc2  to crypto. Spurred on by legislators, something\u8217\'20\'19s got to give.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9jZTFmZjJlM2E4N2RhODAyYmU0OGY5ZjE4YmNkMjdmNy5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200821eg8l0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/19: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, EOS\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,757 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and the altcoins continue to correct but lower levels are likely to attract buyers as the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  macro trend has not changed\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg Intelligence senior strategist Mike McGlone is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/only-something-unexpected-can-stop-bitcoin-price-bull-run-bloomberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  on Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) as he believes that \u8220\'20\'1Csomething unexpected needs to happen for Bitcoin's price to stop doing what it's been doing for most of the past decade: appreciating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, with the S&P 500 hitting a new all-time high today, traders are booking profits in gold and crypto assets. As U.S. markets surge to new highs, Bitcoin price has corrected sharply in the last two days but this is likely to be a short-term blip in a secular uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Veteran investor Jim Rogers thinks that the U.S. stock market is in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/investor-jim-rogers-warned-of-the-worst-economic-downturn-of-his-lifetime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bubble}}}\uc2  and the recent monetary measures by numerous central banks could result in the worst economic meltdown in his lifetime.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/cf99caaf0e05830584da992f4b9c469d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In other news, crypto investment firm Pantera Capital has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/pantera-capital-has-raised-3x-more-this-year-than-it-did-in-2019"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong inflows}}}\uc2  into its Pantera Venture Fund III over the past twelve months, which shows that cryptocurrencies are attracting new investors.\par \par \uc2 However, as the bull market progresses, greed takes over and some traders take excessive risk in order to earn quick returns.\par \par \uc2 Although a few traders might get lucky, most tend to give back their hard-earned gains due to reckless trading. Therefore, traders should be disciplined and stick to their trading principles to generate long-term wealth.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin completed the ascending triangle pattern on Aug. 17 when it closed (UTC time) above $12,113.50 but the bulls could not sustain the breakout and the price dipped back into the triangle on Aug. 18.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8abf0340da93fd097d61ba17f3f4885d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,515), which is an important level to watch out for because the bears have not been able to sustain the price below it since July 22.\par \par \uc2 A strong bounce off this support will show that the bulls continue to buy on dips and if they can propel the price above $12,460, the uptrend is likely to resume.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are sloping higher and the relative strength index is in the positive territory, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink and sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $11,000 and then to $10,400 is possible.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to sustain Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above $444.15 on Aug. 17 attracted profit-booking, which has pulled the price below the breakout level of $415.634.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/278b05bfc68c0cb18521f7ea886dcd5d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($392), it will suggest that the bulls continue to buy on dips and if they can push the price above $415.64, a retest of $446.479 is possible.\par \par \uc2 A breakout above $446.479 can result in a rally to the $480\u8211\'20\'13$500 resistance zone. The upsloping moving averages indicate an advantage to the bulls but the negative divergence on the RSI suggests caution.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that the momentum has weakened and a drop to $366 is possible. Below this support, the correction could extend to the 50-day simple moving average ($314).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not propel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the overhead resistance zone of $0.326113\u8211\'20\'13$0.346727 on Aug. 17, which attracted profit booking by the short-term traders. This has pulled the price down to the 20-day EMA ($0.285).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7095f35b409e16769baab1adb1516f7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the XRP/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will once again attempt to scale the price above the overhead resistance zone. If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to resume.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $0.268478 is possible. If the bulls defend this support, the pair could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 A break below the $0.268478 will be a negative sign that can result in a decline to the 50-day SMA ($0.238).\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) corrected to $14.69 on Aug. 18, which is just below the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $15.053. The bulls have purchased this dip and are currently attempting to resume the uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/97659dd2675fd0928eadfca4a4659d1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can push the price above $17.6738, a retest of the highs at $20.1111 is possible. A breakout of this resistance will signal resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the positive zone, which suggests advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls fail to push the price above $20.1111, a few days of range-bound action is possible. The LINK/USD pair is likely to signal a deeper correction on a break below the $14.69 support.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not propel Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) above the $326.30 resistance on Aug. 17 and 18, which attracted profit booking. This has pulled the altcoin down to the 20-day EMA ($293) and has resulted in the formation of a symmetrical triangle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ea9ffa24706ea7f2e1fb9ba3a15f55aa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink and sustain the BCH/USD pair below the triangle, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($263) and then to $245 is possible. The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI has dropped close to the midpoint, which suggests that the bulls are losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair rebounds off the current levels and breaks above the $326.30 resistance, a retest of $353 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) scaled above the overhead resistance of $65.1573 on Aug. 17 but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. The bears are attempting to fake this breakout and have pulled the altcoin back below $65.1573.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4f19af317a40c0de3b2c06a7ef2e5eb6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the RSI suggests that the momentum has weakened. If the bears can sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($58), a drop to $51 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls defend the 20-day EMA aggressively, the LTC/USD pair will make one more attempt to rise above the $65.1573\u8211\'20\'13$68.9008 resistance. If they succeed, a rally to $80 is likely.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $235.32 on Aug. 18 and broke below the 20-day EMA ($216), which suggests a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/605e2283b7e1b30e21b963a41908e91d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the $200 support, which is just above the 50-day SMA ($198). If the BSV/USD pair rebounds off this level, the bulls will attempt to push the price above the $227\u8211\'20\'13$235.32 resistance zone. If they succeed, a rally to $260 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls fail to push the price above $227, a few days of range-bound action between $200\u8211\'20\'13$227 is likely. A break below $200 could signal weakness and result in a fall to $160.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) slipped below the $0.13\u8211\'20\'13$0.15 zone today but the bears have not been able to sustain the lower levels, which suggests some buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/456c93011562862cf870ad3fdd7ecb18.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.137) has flattened out and the RSI has dipped below the 50 level, which points to a possible consolidation in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 A breakdown and close (UTC time) below $0.13 will signal a possible change in trend. Below this support, a drop to the $0.11\u8211\'20\'13$0.10 zone is likely.\par \par \uc2 The next leg of the uptrend is likely to start after the bulls push the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair above the $0.15\u8211\'20\'13$0.1543051 resistance.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the $22.93\u8211\'20\'13$24.4588 resistance zone on Aug. 17 and has dipped to the 20-day EMA ($22).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/405408227c1813131d0ef887d55365fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the BNB/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance zone. If they succeed, a rally to $27.1905 is likely.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink the pair below the 20-day EMA a fall to $20.50 is possible. Below this level, the correction could deepen to the 50-day SMA ($19.58). The negative divergence on the RSI signals a weakening momentum.\par \par \uc2 EOS/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/eos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EOS}}}\uc2  could not sustain above the $3.8811 resistance on Aug. 17, which resulted in profit booking by the short-term traders. The altcoin corrected to $3.3086 today, which is just above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $3.2766 and the 20-day EMA ($3.264).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/73cd49543fcd894afcdc2bfb5892765e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EOS/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 EOS/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/EOSUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Usually, in a strong uptrend, the corrections end between the 38.2% and 50% Fibonacci retracement levels because the bulls are in a hurry to buy and they do not wait for a deeper fall.\par \par \uc2 However, a sharper fall to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level or below it suggests that the momentum has weakened. The critical support to watch on the downside is $3.2766 and the breakout level of $3.1104. A break below this support will be a huge negative.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls defend the 20-day EMA, the EOS/USD pair will again attempt to rise to the $3.8811\u8211\'20\'13$3.95 resistance zone. A break above this zone will signal the possible resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy80NTg4Njc4MjY1MDcwZmU2Njg1MWE0MmJiMDE3ZTUyMS5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200819eg8j000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/17: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , EOS, BNB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,703 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s strong move above the $12,200 resistance could boost sentiment and lead to a stronger rally in select altcoins\par \par \uc2 Investors usually buy large quantities of gold when they do not have faith in fiat currencies and want to protect their purchasing power against debasement. Berkshire Hathaway\u8217\'20\'19s recent purchase of Canadian gold miner Barrick Gold {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cointelegraph.com/news/warren-buffett-buying-gold-may-push-bitcoin-to-50k-investors-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggests that Warren Buffet is not confident}}}\uc2  about the future health of the United States and global economy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/buffett-bought-gold-will-buy-bitcoin-morgan-creek-digital-co-founder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Morgan Creek Digital co-founder and partner Jason Williams believes}}}\uc2  that although Buffet might not directly invest in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), it is likely that one of the younger managers will.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/72c6faf4ff417d1175e640b4d21f7ffa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 With gold making a sharp move today, Bitcoin has also followed it higher, which shows that their correlation in the short term might be increasing once again.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale Investments has also widened its offering after its Bitcoin Cash Trust and Litecoin Trust {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-brings-altcoins-to-over-the-counter-trading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received the green light}}}\uc2  to deposit at the \uc2 Depository Trust Company\uc2 . This enables the products to list on major U.S. stock exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at some of the strongest crypto assets to see where they might go this week.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke out of its overhead resistance at $12,113.50, and if the bulls can close (UTC time) the price above this resistance, the ascending triangle pattern will complete.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7d27b6d5d916d9f7f78f96c37225ee65.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a pattern target of $13,702.55, which is just below the June 26, 2019 high at $13,973.50. If the price reaches this level, it may act as a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 Currently, both moving averages are rising, and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the overbought zone, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to sustain the price above $12,113.50, Bitcoin's price could drop to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($11,457). A break below this support will be the first indication that momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been sustaining above the $415.634 level for the past few days, which is a positive sign. This suggests that the bulls are not waiting for a deeper correction to buy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/6b3d03b79a88072a63dd5b70c1d1c44e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the price above $444.15, the uptrend is likely to resume. The next target is the $480\u8211\'20\'13$500 zone. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest that the trend favors the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below $415.634, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($387) is possible. If the ETH/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again attempt to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 A break below the 20-day EMA will be the first sign of weakening momentum and a break below $366 could tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has picked up momentum after breaking out of the falling wedge pattern on Aug. 14. The bulls will now try to push the price above the $0.326113\u8211\'20\'13$0.346727 overhead resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0aab8b1b98055708ef399bdcb84e339b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, a rally to $0.40 is possible. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought territory indicates advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the overhead resistance zone, then the XRP/USD pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 A breakdown below the 20-day EMA ($0.28) will be the first sign of weakness. The trend will turn in favor of the bears if the pair plummets below $0.268478.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's LINK continues to be in a strong uptrend. Since the start of this leg of the up move on July 30, the altcoin has not corrected for three days in a row, which shows that the bulls are buying on every minor dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/3d15486510a9125966d43c7e2516e784.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The sharp rally of the past few days has pushed the RSI above the 80 levels, which suggests that the LINK/USD pair is heavily overbought in the near term. However, this alone is not a reason to fall because in May 2019 the RSI topped out close to 90.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls push the price above $20.1111, the uptrend can extend to $21.60 and then to $24.18. However, vertical rallies usually witness waterfall declines. Hence, traders should be careful not to be swayed by greed.\par \par \uc2 On the downside, a break below $16 could be the first sign that momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has broken out of the downtrend line, which invalidates a developing descending triangle pattern. The 20-day EMA ($292) is sloping up, and the RSI has risen close to the overbought zone, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d422f8108eedc193a835bc3214209040.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to push the price to $326.30 and then to $353. A breakout of this resistance is likely to result in a rally to $410 and then to $430.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears defend the overhead resistance at $353, the BCH/USD pair might extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The trend will turn in favor of the bears if the pair turns down and breaks below the $280 support.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) picked up momentum after breaking above the descending channel on Aug. 15. The bulls are currently attempting to push the price above the overhead resistance at $65.1573.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a69175b59d71d70c51bd653b3450ea6d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($57) has started to slope up once again, and the RSI is close to the overbought zone, which suggests that the bulls are again back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above $65.1573 is likely to start the next leg of the up move to $80 and then to $84.\par \par \uc2 However, if the LTC/USD pair turns down from the current levels, it could drop to the 20-day EMA. A break below this support could sink the price to $51.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke above the downtrend line on Aug. 15, but the bulls have not been able to pick up momentum, which shows a lack of demand at higher levels. The altcoin is currently facing resistance at $227.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/1b2f99dd740bb5c68ddf29bb813b67be.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, a minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the BSV/USD pair to slip below the 20-day EMA ($217). If the bulls can push the price above $227, a rally to $260.86 is likely. A breakout of this resistance could extend the rally to $320.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $200 is possible. A break below this support will shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) remains range-bound between the $0.13\u8211\'20\'13$0.15 zone, which suggests a balance between supply and demand. It is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout, hence traders should wait for the price to make a decisive move before entering any trades.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b66b7b7a406e94801dcd0553b57f942e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 50-day SMA is sloping up, which suggests that the medium-term trend remains in favor of the bulls. If the buyers can propel the price above $0.1543051, the next leg of the up move is likely to start. The next target to watch out for is $0.20.\par \par \uc2 If the bears defend the overhead resistance at $0.1543051, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could extend its stay inside the range.\par \par \uc2 A breakdown and close (UTC time) below $0.13 will signal the possible start of a deeper correction to the $0.11\u8211\'20\'13$0.10 support zone.\par \par \uc2 EOS/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/eos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EOS}}}\uc2  above the overhead resistance at $3.8811, but the bears are defending this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages have turned up, and the RSI is in the overbought zone, suggesting advantage to the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2fba1c4f77db30a2ffd233ba9263d57e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EOS/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 EOS/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/EOSUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the price above $3.8811, a rally to $4.85 and then to $5.40 is possible. There is a minor resistance at $4.40 and again at $4.60, but both these are likely to be crossed.\par \par \uc2 However, if the EOS/USD pair turns down from the current levels, a minor consolidation or correction is possible. The momentum might weaken if the bears sink the pair below the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $3.4052.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is facing resistance in the $22.93\u8211\'20\'13$24.4588 resistance zone; however, the positive sign is that the bulls have managed to keep the price above $22.93 for the past two days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9b25dab45c02ab227e3d6f416a0b4f01.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are sloping up, and the RSI is in the positive zone, suggesting advantage to the bulls. Above $24.4588, a rally to $27.1905 is possible. The bears are likely to defend this resistance aggressively, but if this level is scaled, the next target is $32.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the BNB/USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $20.50.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9jYTM5M2ExYWUwZTk2NTdhYTQzNGFiNTRmZmQ1ZWE0MC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200817eg8h000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/14: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, BSV, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,649 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Traders have turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Ethereum again and the strong break above $400 could pull Bitcoin and other altcoins higher\par \par \uc2 Data from Grayscale Investments shows that the firm\u8217\'20\'19s assets under management {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/interest-in-grayscale-crypto-products-not-easing-up-not-just-btc-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared}}}\uc2  from about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1588489/000156459020038402/gbtc-10q_20200630.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.9 billion}}}\uc2  at the end of 2019 to over $3.5 billion by the end of June 30, 2020.\par \par \uc2 The correction in the U.S. dollar (DXY) and the possibility of further weakness due to continued money printing by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  could be one of the main reasons for the surge in institutions investing in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/wall-street-starts-hodling-bitcoin-as-40-of-btc-unmoved-in-2-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40%}}}\uc2  of the Bitcoin accumulated over the past two years has not been moved, which suggests that investors are \u8220\'20\'1CHODLing\u8221\'20\'1D their purchases as they anticipate higher levels in the future.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d10aa2360b85be810952eaea95b1af36.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Abra CEO Bill Barhydt believes that Bitcoin is witnessing a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/abra-ceo-explains-why-it-s-bitcoin-s-time-to-shine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pivotal moment}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D as a new asset class. Rumors suggest that the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  could try to revive growth by stoking inflation. Hence, Barhydt considers that this is the best time for Bitcoin to stake a claim \u8220\'20\'1Cas the defacto hard \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bounced off the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,253) on Aug. 12, which shows that the bulls are aggressively buying the dips to this support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/6dfe4bd7822243aeb47cc6f39ae4b8dd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price action of the past few days has formed an ascending triangle pattern, which will complete on a breakout and close (UTC time) above $12,113.50. The target objective of this set up is $13,702.55.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the relative strength index is in positive territory, which suggests that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the BTC/USD pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance of $12,113.50 and breaks below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Such a move will be the first sign of profit booking at higher levels. Below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $10,400 is possible. If this support holds, the pair might remain range-bound for a few days. The trend will turn negative on a break below the $10,400\u8211\'20\'13$10,000 support zone.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) surged above the downtrend line and the overhead resistance of $415.634 on Aug. 13, which shows that the uptrend has resumed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/447fc128d2e931dee73d1e0d73404e95.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the overbought zone, suggesting advantage to the bulls. The next target on the upside is $480 and then $520.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be negated if the bears fake the current breakout and pull the ETH/USD pair down below $415.634. Such a move will indicate profit booking at higher levels and could result in a deeper pullback.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has broken out of the falling wedge pattern, which is a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign. If the bulls can scale the price above $0.307301, a rally to the $0.326113\u8211\'20\'13$0.346727 resistance zone is likely. A breakout above this zone will signal a resumption of the uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/68665f0eafd96bc9b349125feb096e0e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Above $0.346727, the next target to watch out for is $0.40. The uptrending moving averages and the RSI close to the overbought zone suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the XRP/USD pair turns down from $0.307301, the bears will make another attempt to sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.275). If they succeed, a deeper correction to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.244472 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 261.8% Fibonacci extension level of $17.4319 on Aug. 13 but the bulls could not sustain the price above it, which suggests some profit booking at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2a41fb89107801c299303bcd0ce04287.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the LINK/USD pair has not given up much ground, which suggests that the majority of the bulls are still holding on to their positions as they expect the rally to continue. If the buyers can push the price above $18.3488, the rally can extend to $20.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, selling could pick up momentum on a break below $15.9175. Below this level, a drop to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $13.9639 is possible.\par \par \uc2 If the pair bounces off this level, the bulls will again attempt to resume the uptrend but a break below this level could signal that the momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has held the $280 support for the past few days, which suggests that the bulls are buying at these levels. However, unless the bulls push the price above the downtrend line, the bears will again try to break the $280 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/d68d2a7cd4d1f7670b78fa8f9b0d8355.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price again turns down from the downtrend line, it will form a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  descending triangle pattern, which will complete on a breakdown and close (UTC time) below $280. The pattern target of this setup is $222.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls push the price above the downtrend line, a move to $325 and then to $353 is possible. A breakout of this resistance will signal the possible resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) has held the $200 support but the rebound lacks strength, which shows a lack of urgency among the bulls to buy at these levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/156ccbab3553b2e76a3285b6276c7015.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price has reached the downtrend line, which is likely to act as a stiff resistance. If the BSV/USD pair turns down from this resistance, the possibility of a break below $200 and the 50-day simple moving average ($192) increases. Below the level, the decline can extend to $160.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the 20-day EMA ($214) is flat and the RSI is close to the midpoint, which shows a balance between supply and demand. A breakout above the downtrend line and the $227 resistance will signal that bulls are making a comeback. Above this level, a retest of $260.86 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully defended the breakout level of $51, which is a positive sign. If they can push \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) above the descending channel, a move to $60 and then to $65.1573 is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/9e018e51a8d58d08f7711a6509b75b4e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break above $65.1573 could result in a rally to $80. The LTC/USD pair is presently above the 20-day EMA ($55) and the RSI has risen to just under 60 level, which suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from the current levels, then the bears will make another attempt to sink the price below $51. A break below the 50-day SMA ($48) will be a huge negative.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is currently consolidating between the $0.13\u8211\'20\'13$0.15 zone. The attempt by the bears to break below this zone on Aug. 12 was purchased aggressively by the bulls, which shows strong demand at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/37e331c346c45a6f9855a1fe51ee79ea.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 During this leg of the up move, twice the consolidations lasted for about 27 days or more. The current consolidation has completed 18 days and if history were to repeat itself, the price might remain stuck in the range for a few more days before a breakout or a breakdown happens.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.137) has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which also suggests a balance between the bulls and bears. The next trending move is likely to start after the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair closes (UTC time) above $0.15 or below $0.13.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the 20-day EMA ($21.37) on Aug. 11, 12 and 13 but on all three days, the bears could not sustain the lower levels, which shows aggressive buying by the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ec0b687274433c617044c4f3a7de4c96.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Today, the bulls have pushed the price above the downtrend line and are attempting to scale the overhead resistance of $22.93. If they succeed, a rally to $24.588 and then to $27.1905 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are rising and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the BNB/USD pair turns down from $22.93, the bears will make another attempt to break the 20-day EMA support.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) is consolidating in an uptrend, which is a positive sign. Currently, the price is stuck between $0.154322 and $0.176596.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/6cd91a9b96f85866760582a88389a4d9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.16) is sloping up marginally and the RSI is close to the 60 level, which suggests that the momentum has weakened but the advantage is still with the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $0.176596, the uptrend is likely to resume with the next target at $0.20. Conversely, if the CRO/USD pair plummets below the support of the range, a drop to $0.13 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9kY2ZhYjY3YzU4MDQ3ZjNiYjljYzAxZGQ2YjExNDEyMy5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200814eg8e000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/12: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, BSV, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XTZ, BNB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,850 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As Bitcoin price slowly regains momentum, many altcoins have been rewarding traders by rallying to new all-time highs\par \par \uc2 On August 11 \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest publicly traded business intelligence company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/worlds-biggest-business-intelligence-firm-buys-21k-btc-for-250m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced that it had ditched fiat currency and built its primary treasury reserve with Bitcoin}}}\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s CEO \uc2 Michael J. Saylor\uc2  believes that the coronavirus pandemic and the stimulus measures enacted to counter it will cause \u8220\'20\'1Ca significant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-reasons-why-microstrategy-adopted-bitcoin-and-why-others-will-too"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 depreciating effect}}}\uc2  on the long-term real value of fiat currencies and many other conventional asset types.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Saylor further explained that Bitcoin \u8220\'20\'1Cis a dependable store of value and an attractive investment asset with more long-term appreciation potential than holding cash.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/73618c6f160a888fc2f03dfafa780d21.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 On similar lines, BitGo CEO Mike Belshe also warned that the aggressive money printing will devalue fiat currencies and make them worthless to holders. Belshe urged investors to invest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/invest-3-in-bitcoin-to-avoid-covid-19-lockdown-devaluation-bitgo-ceo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 3%}}}\uc2  of their portfolio in Bitcoin because it is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe lowest risk, highest asymmetric upside investment\u8221\'20\'1D many will see in their lifetime.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls again failed to propel Bitcoin above the overhead resistance of $12,113.50 on Aug. 10, and this resulted in profit booking by short-term traders. The correction pulled the price down to the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,127) but the bears could not break this support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a218dc0d821407b393bb0b67adf4d65d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This shows that the bulls are aggressively buying the dips to the 20-day EMA support. In an uptrend, when the price bounces off the 20-day EMA, it usually increases the possibility that the uptrend will resume.\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair closes (UTC time) above $12,113.50, the momentum is likely to pick up and a quick move to $13,000 is possible. The bears are likely to defend this level, which can result in a minor consolidation or correction, but if the bulls do not give up much ground, the uptrend is likely to extend to $14,000.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the pair below the critical support zone of $10,400\u8211\'20\'13$10,000.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) remains positive as the price has held above the critical support at $366 for the past few days. This shows that the bulls are accumulating on dips to this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/2d393c2af381f71589932a47aabadd5a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are rising and the relative strength index is in the positive zone, which shows that the bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 A break above the downtrend line will signal strength and the momentum is likely to pick up above $415.634. Above this level, the uptrend can reach $480.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the ETH/USD pair reverses direction from the downtrend line and plummets below the 20-day EMA ($357). Below this support, the correction can extend to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $304.367.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls had pushed the price above the falling wedge on Aug. 11 but they could not sustain the higher levels. The bears used this to their advantage and sold aggressively, dragging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  below the wedge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/5d5440e8e35f7e33197dfe43c408f723.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls purchased the dip to the 20-day EMA ($0.27) and are currently attempting to push the price back above $0.284584. If they succeed, it will be a positive sign.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside. A break above the wedge and the $0.307301 resistance will signal strength and increase the possibility of a rally to $0.326113.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the XRP/USD pair turns down from the resistance and breaks below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) remains in a strong uptrend as the correction from the $14.4586 level only lasted for two days on Aug. 10 and 11. During this, the bears could not even break below the immediate support of $12, which shows that the bulls are aggressively buying the dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8f16bbebb33960971d3dab39959f7e7f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The sharp bounce off the $12 levels has already pushed the LINK/USD pair above the $14.4586\u8211\'20\'13$14.8537 resistance zone. The next target is the 261.8% Fibonacci extension level of $17.4319 and if this level is also scaled, then the next level to watch out for is $20.\par \par \uc2 However, as the pair hits new highs, the RSI has again risen into deeply overbought levels. Although the RSI can remain overbought for an extended period of time, vertical rallies rarely sustain. Therefore, traders can consider trailing the stops on their positions instead of becoming greedy.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($284) and the $280 support on Aug. 11, but a minor positive is that the bulls managed to close (UTC time) the day at $281.87.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/fb8bdb8a38cc6fd967bc3bc897421d5d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Today, the bears again attempted to resume the down move by plunging the BCH/USD pair below $270. However, the bulls bought the dip and have pushed the price back above $280, which is a minor positive.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand. A break above the downtrend line will be the first sign that the advantage might be shifting in favor of the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the pair breaks and closes (UTC time) below $280. Such a move could drag the price to $260.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure to push the price higher attracted profit-booking by the traders on Aug. 11, which resulted in a break below the 20-day EMA ($214). The bulls are currently attempting to keep Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the $200 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e5564c5bd2828956f5495bfc2ffad295.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Any bounce from the $200 level will face resistance at the downtrend line and again at $227. If the BSV/USD pair turns down from this resistance, a few days of consolidation between $200\u8211\'20\'13$227 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flat and the RSI is just below the 50 level, which points towards a possible range-bound action in the near term.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from either resistance and breaks below $200, it will be a huge negative and could result in a drop to $160.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) broke below the $56\u8211\'20\'13$60 range and the 20-day EMA ($54.70) on Aug. 11, which resulted in a retest of the breakout level of $51. The altcoin has bounced off this support, which is a positive sign as it shows that the bulls are attempting to defend this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/4e5d19fb33c4fbc28d9c8b7853325516.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is close to the midpoint, which suggests a range-bound action for a few days.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, a break and close (UTC time) above the descending channel will be the first sign of strength. This will increase the possibility of a rally to $60 and then to $65.1573. The uptrend is likely to resume if the LTC/USD pair sustains above $65.1573.\par \par \uc2 The trend will turn in favor of the bears if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $51.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.137) on Aug. 11 and the bears capitalized on this opportunity by pushing the price below the $0.13 support today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/aa1a96130fc53a67316ea3e4f563ef19.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls aggressively purchased the dip to the 50-day simple moving average ($0.121) and pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair back above the $0.13 level. This is a positive sign as it suggests a rejection of the breakdown below $0.13.\par \par \uc2 The flattening 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the 50 level point to a possible consolidation in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 The trend will turn positive on a breakout and close (UTC time) above the overhead resistance of $0.1543051. Conversely, a break below the 50-day SMA will signal a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 XTZ/USD\par \par \uc2 Tezos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/tezos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XTZ}}}\uc2  ) broke above the stiff overhead resistance at $3.96 on Aug. 10 and made a new high, which is always a sign of strength as it shows that the bulls are keen to buy at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/a1dcebc5f61983e3ecf1978bc5c7e9c6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XTZ/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XTZ/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XTZUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears attempted to fake this breakout on Aug. 11 when they tried to sink the price back below the breakout level of $3.96. However, the bulls again purchased the dips aggressively, which helped the price recover from the intraday low of $3.75 and close (UTC time) at $4.01.\par \par \uc2 Today, the bears again attempted to sink the XTZ/USD pair but the bulls used the opportunity to buy at lower levels. The aggressive buying has already propelled the pair to new highs.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can close (UTC time) the price above $4.50, the next level to watch for is the 200% Fibonacci extension level of $4.8766 and then 261.8% extension level of $5.57. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair reverses direction and plunges below $3.60.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The $21.7628\u8211\'20\'13$22.93 range resolved to the downside on Aug. 11 as Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) plunged to $20.66, but the positive thing is that the bears have not been able to sustain the price below the 20-day EMA ($21.16).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ce83d8ced1e03cafcca600ad0d77e3e8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This shows that the sentiment is to buy the dips and the bulls are aggressively defending the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price back above $21.7628 and sustain the higher levels, it will be a positive sign. That will suggest a rejection of the recent breakdown and could signal a resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI has dropped below the 60 level, which suggests that the momentum has weakened marginally but the advantage remains with the bulls.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the BNB/USD pair turns down from the current levels and plummets below the trendline. Below this support, a drop to $18.20 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy85MWVmMDQ0ZWE0MGJlZDNiODkzYzEzMTVhY2M4Y2JhZi5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200812eg8c000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/10: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BSV, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price continues to decline at $12,000, but altcoins have taken advantage of the range bound action by rallying higher\par \par \uc2 Traders prefer to trade a trending market, as it generally moves in one direction and the retracements offer low-risk entry opportunities. This is because a trade that follows the major trend carries a greater possibility of earning profits than one in a volatile market.\par \par \uc2 As several cryptocurrencies started a trending move in July, web traffic to the crypto exchanges also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/web-traffic-on-global-crypto-exchanges-surged-13-in-july"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  by 13%, according to data from ICO Analytics.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8611f028884bf0fc7e370f62f50606b1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The derivatives market also comes alive when the underlying market is trending as professional traders use leverage to make quick profits using the futures and options route. This could be one of the reasons for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-options-data-suggests-pro-traders-expect-eth-price-to-break-400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sustained increase}}}\uc2  in Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) options open interest over the past three months.\par \par \uc2 Several reasons can be attributed to the start of a trending move in an asset class. Max Keiser believes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cointelegraph.com/news/capital-flight-out-of-asia-is-taking-bitcoin-express-says-max-keiser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 capital fleeing Asia}}}\uc2  is one of the main reasons for the sharp rally in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the major cryptocurrencies to find out whether the uptrend is likely to resume or if it time for a correction to start.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push Bitcoin above the overhead resistance of $12,113.50, which is a positive sign. This suggests that the bulls are not booking profits yet, which is frustrating the traders who have been left out because they are forced to buy at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ed95947e0477c33be06d00bcef419c7a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the relative strength index is in the overbought zone, which suggests that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (in UTC) above $12,113.50 is likely to resume the uptrend. There is a minor resistance at $12,304.37, but that is likely to be crossed. Above this level, the uptrend can reach $13,000, and above it, $14,000.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears aggressively defend the $12,113.50 level, the BTC/USD pair might correct to the 20-day exponential moving average of $11,052. A strong bounce off this level will increase the possibility of a break above the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, it will signal weakness. Below this level, a retest of the $10,400 level is possible. A drop below this support will signal that the bears are back in the game.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether has been trading above the breakout level of $366 for the past few days \u8212\'20\'14 a huge positive, as it shows that the bulls are not hurrying to liquidate their positions. This suggests that the bulls expect the uptrend to continue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e5af1b9a16f384776d9ef9fed4a6503a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the overbought zone, indicating that the path of least resistance is to the upside. A breakout and close above $415.634 will signal a resumption of the uptrend toward the next target of $480.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears defend the $415.634 resistance, the ETH/USD pair might spend some more time inside the range.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below $366. Such a move will suggest a weakening momentum that can drag the price to the 20-day EMA of $351. A break below this support could signal a deeper correction to 61.8% and a Fibonacci retracement level of $304.367.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  is currently trading inside a falling wedge pattern, which usually acts as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. If the bulls can push the price above the wedge, the uptrend is likely to resume with the first target at $0.346727 and then $0.432105.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/91ef4ead4a5148e277b01681c8a4be26.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The correction from $0.326113 has been healthy, as it has pulled down the RSI from deeply overbought levels. Both moving averages are sloping upward, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the wedge and the 20-day EMA ($0.267). Such a move will be a negative sign that can drag the XRP/USD pair to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.244472.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) dipped to the 20-day EMA of $284 on Aug. 7 and again on Aug. 10, suggesting that the bears are attempting to sink the price back below the breakout level of $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b10fd524033b314e4dd58c284780d0fd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will be a huge negative, as it will indicate a lack of demand at higher levels. Such a move could result in a fall to $260 and then to $245.\par \par \uc2 However, the 20-day EMA is gradually sloping up and the RSI has been sustaining above 60, which suggests a slight advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, it will signal advantage to the bulls. Above this resistance, a rally to $353 is possible. A breakout of this level could resume the uptrend to $400.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) dipped on Aug. 7 to $9.05, but the bears could not sustain the lower levels. By close, the price had recovered sharply from the intraday lows, which shows aggressive buying by the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/07dfe75d3ca6c7307a4dba8184f70165.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This move seems to have caught the aggressive bears on the wrong side, and they were forced to cover their short positions as the price broke out to new highs, which resulted in a strong rally on Aug. 8 and 9.\par \par \uc2 The LINK/USD pair rose to a high of $14.4586 on Aug. 9, which is just below the 200% Fibonacci extension level of $14.8537. The bears are likely to mount a stiff resistance in the $14.4586\u8211\'20\'13$14.8537 zone, while the RSI has also risen into the deep overbought zone, suggesting a minor consolidation or correction.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls continue to buy at higher levels and push the price above the resistance zone, a rally to the 261.8% Fibonacci extension level of $17.4319 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to push Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the $240 resistance, which suggests a lack of demand at higher levels. However, on the downside, the bulls are buying the dips to $214.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/97347ef05d2c4808f3fd9bb5385afa5a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA of $216 is flattening out and the RSI is gradually falling, which suggests that the bulls are losing their grip. If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA and the $214 support zone, a drop to $200 is possible.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the BSV/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will once again attempt to push the price above $240. If successful, a move to $260.86 is likely.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has roughly been trading between the $56\u8211\'20\'13$60 level since Aug. 2. This suggests a balance between demand and supply. However, as both moving averages are rising and the RSI is in the positive zone, the advantage is with the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/0f5569fb31a826af300990c70676e034.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the LTC/USD pair rises above $60, the advantage will shift in favor of the bulls. Above this level, a rally to $65.1573 is possible. This is the critical level to watch out for because, if the bulls can propel the price above this level, the momentum is likely to pick up.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears sink the pair below $56 and the 20-day EMA ($54.83), a drop to the critical support at $51 is possible. A break below this support will signal a possible change in trend but if the bulls buy the dip to this support, the pair might remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) turned down from the $0.15\u8211\'20\'13$0.1543051 resistance zone on Aug. 9, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this zone. However, the upsloping moving averages suggest that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/f0c83bb607ac30f064342fa6a3aed2d5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 /USD daily chart}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA of $0.1379, the bulls will make one more attempt to scale the price above the zone. If they succeed, a rally to $0.173 and then to $0.20 is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to the $0.13 support is likely. A bounce off this support could keep the pair range-bound for a few more days. A break below $0.13 is likely to shift the advantage in favor of the bears, with the next support at $0.12.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside the tight range of $21.7628-$22.93 for the past three days, showing uncertainty among both bulls and bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/7fb606d6b16f83621a908c40f6f06d49.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 While the bulls are buying the dips to $21.7628, the bears are defending the overhead resistance at $22.93.\par \par \uc2 However, the moving averages are sloping up and the RSI remains in the positive zone, suggesting advantage to the bulls. If the bulls can push the price above $22.93, a move to $24.4588 and then to $27.1905 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below $21.7628, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($21) is likely. A break below this support will signal a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD\par \par \uc2 Crypto.com Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/crypto-com-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO}}}\uc2  ) remains in an uptrend, but it is facing resistance near the highs at $0.176596. Hence, it is likely to consolidate between $0.176596 and $0.154322 for a few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/fb606fdf1156b9132d7919958d92daae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 CRO/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/CROUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The RSI is showing signs of forming a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence, which indicates that the momentum is weakening. If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.159), it will indicate profit booking and a break below $0.154322 will shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 This assumption of a correction will be invalidated if the CRO/USD pair continues higher and breaks above $0.176596. Above this level, the next level to watch out for is $0.20.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/528_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy8xY2MxNTBkOTVmN2E0NWVkODUxNzY5OTI5OGI1ZGVjOC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020200811eg8a0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price Analysis 8/10: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BSV, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, CRO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,870 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price continues to decline at $12,000, but altcoins have taken advantage of the range bound action by rallying higher\par \par \uc2 Traders prefer to trade a trending market as it generally moves in one direction and the retracements offer low-risk entry opportunities. This is because a trade that follows the major trend carries a greater possibility of earning profits than one in a volatile market.\par \par \uc2 As several cryptocurrencies started a trending move in July, web traffic to the crypto exchanges also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/web-traffic-on-global-crypto-exchanges-surged-13-in-july"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  by 13%, according to data from ICO Analytics.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/8611f028884bf0fc7e370f62f50606b1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/sharing/0-pl0nevx5n8_1591987263073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The derivatives market also comes alive when the underlying market is trending as professional traders use leverage to make quick profits using the futures and options route. This could be one of the reasons for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-options-data-suggests-pro-traders-expect-eth-price-to-break-400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sustained increase}}}\uc2  in Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) options open interest over the past three months.\par \par \uc2 Several reasons can be attributed to the start of a trending move in an asset class. Max Keiser believes that capital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/capital-flight-out-of-asia-is-taking-bitcoin-express-says-max-keiser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fleeing}}}\uc2  Asia is one of the main reasons for the sharp rally in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the major cryptocurrencies to find out whether the uptrend is likely to resume or is it time for a correction to start.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push Bitcoin above the overhead resistance of $12,113.50, which is a positive sign. This suggests that the bulls are not booking profits yet, which is frustrating the traders who have been left out because they are forced to buy at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/ed95947e0477c33be06d00bcef419c7a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the relative strength index is in the overbought zone, which suggests that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above $12,113.50 is likely to resume the uptrend. There is a minor resistance at $12,304.37 but that is likely to be crossed. Above this level, the uptrend can reach $13,000 and above it $14,000.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears aggressively defend the $12,113.50 level, the BTC/USD pair might correct to the 20-day exponential moving average ($11,052). A strong bounce off this level will increase the possibility of a break above the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, it will signal weakness. Below this level a retest of the $10,400 level is possible. A drop below this support will signal that the bears are back in the game.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been trading above the breakout level of $366 for the past few days, which is a huge positive as it shows that the bulls are not hurrying to liquidate their positions. This suggests that the bulls expect the uptrend to continue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/e5af1b9a16f384776d9ef9fed4a6503a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the overbought zone, which indicates that the path of least resistance is to the upside. A breakout and close (UTC time) above $415.634 will signal a resumption of the uptrend towards the next target of $480.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bears defend the $415.634 resistance, the ETH/USD pair might spend some more time inside the range.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below $366. Such a move will suggest a weakening momentum that can drag the price to the 20-day EMA ($351). A break below this support could signal a deeper correction to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $304.367.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  is currently trading inside a falling wedge pattern, which usually acts as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. If the bulls can push the price above the wedge, the uptrend is likely to resume with the first target at $0.346727 and then $0.432105.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/91ef4ead4a5148e277b01681c8a4be26.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The correction from $$0.326113 has been healthy as it has pulled down the RSI from deeply overbought levels. Both moving averages are sloping up, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the wedge and the 20-day EMA ($0.267). Such a move will be a negative sign that can drag the XRP/USD pair to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.244472.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) dipped to the 20-day EMA ($284) on Aug. 7 and again on Aug. 10, which suggests that the bears are attempting to sink the price back below the breakout level of $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/b10fd524033b314e4dd58c284780d0fd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will be a huge negative as it will indicate a lack of demand at higher levels. Such a move could result in a fall to $260 and then to $245.\par \par \uc2 However